IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei1-interpretation`
IMPORT `ei1-qualifying`
IMPORT `ei1-payment`
IMPORT `ei1-benefit-period`
IMPORT `ei1-rate`
IMPORT `ei1-disentitlement-deductions`
IMPORT `ei1-illness-pregnancy`
IMPORT `ei1-parental`
IMPORT `ei1-caring`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part I, sections 6 to 23.3(5) -- THE SEAT LAYER (piece ei1).
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30; nothing here is
-- verified against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has lost work, or cannot work because of sickness, pregnancy, caring for a child or a family
-- member, asking whether they qualify for Employment Insurance benefits, how many hours or weeks they need, how much
-- they would receive and for how long, and what they must do or tell the Commission. The Commission and the Ministers
-- have no seat: what they must pay, decide or may do appears here only as what the person is owed or exposed to.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs (yes/no, numbers, dates, and the modules' own choices), one per fact the
-- person can state, each @desc worded as the person would be asked. The lists and records that the layer-1 modules expect
-- (violations, earlier benefit periods, the special benefits paid, the weeks of earnings) are built inside each question,
-- in its WHERE, and the SAME module rule is then called; no rule is restated here. Three choices are assumed, not ruled
-- (NOTES.md, fork register, F-seat-*):
--   * a violation is asked about once (the one of the highest class), not as a list (F-seat-violation);
--   * up to five earlier benefit periods are asked about, each by the day it began; one yes/no says whether the person
--     was notified of payment or non-payment for a week in the 260 weeks, and it is applied to each earlier period
--     (F-seat-earlier);
--   * the weeks of earnings in the qualifying period are not asked week by week: the person states the total of their
--     highest-earning weeks, and s 14(4) (which picks those weeks) is not called here (F-seat-weeks).
-- Figures that other pieces or the Regulations supply (the tables of Schedules I, IV and V, the regional rate, the maximum
-- yearly insurable earnings, the prescribed reductions for provincial benefits) are inputs, and a change in any of them
-- changes the answers.
-- Judgments the Act hands to the Commission ("in the opinion of the Commission", "the Commission is satisfied") are asked
-- as facts about what the Commission has found or directed, never worked out here.
-- Where a group arises only in a situation the person may not be in, its heading comment says so.

§ `Employment Insurance Act, Part I (sections 6 to 23.3) -- the claimant's questions`

§§ `Who I am, and whether a job is suitable (section 6)`

-- Section 6(1): the two kinds of claimant; section 6(4) and (5): when a job offered is not suitable employment.

-- s 6(1) "disentitled": not entitled under section 13, 18, 21, 31, 32, 33, 36, 37, 49 or 50 or under the regulations. Sections 31 to 37, 49 and 50 are in another piece of this encoding, so each is asked as a fact.
@export Am I disentitled from receiving benefits (s 6(1))?
GIVEN `I am not entitled under section 13` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not entitled to be paid benefits under section 13 (you have not yet served your waiting period)?
      `I am not entitled under section 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not entitled to be paid benefits under section 18 (you failed to prove availability for a working day)?
      `I am not entitled under section 21` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not entitled to be paid benefits under section 21 (a minor attachment claimant off work through illness)?
      `I am not entitled under section 31` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not entitled to be paid benefits under section 31?
      `I am not entitled under section 32` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not entitled to be paid benefits under section 32?
      `I am not entitled under section 33` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not entitled to be paid benefits under section 33?
      `I am not entitled under section 36` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not entitled to be paid benefits under section 36?
      `I am not entitled under section 37` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not entitled to be paid benefits under section 37?
      `I am not entitled under section 49` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not entitled to be paid benefits under section 49?
      `I am not entitled under section 50` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not entitled to be paid benefits under section 50?
      `I am not entitled under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not entitled to be paid benefits under the Regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I disentitled from receiving benefits` IF
    `s 6(1) disentitled` `I am not entitled under section 13` `I am not entitled under section 18` `I am not entitled under section 21` `I am not entitled under section 31` `I am not entitled under section 32` `I am not entitled under section 33` `I am not entitled under section 36` `I am not entitled under section 37` `I am not entitled under section 49` `I am not entitled under section 50` `I am not entitled under the regulations`

-- s 6(1) "disqualified": disqualified under section 27 or 30.
@export Am I disqualified from receiving benefits (s 6(1))?
GIVEN `I am disqualified under section 27` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you disqualified from receiving benefits under section 27?
      `I am disqualified under section 30` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you disqualified from receiving benefits under section 30?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I disqualified from receiving benefits` IF
    `s 6(1) disqualified` `I am disqualified under section 27` `I am disqualified under section 30`

-- s 6(1) "initial claim for benefits": a claim made for the purpose of establishing my benefit period.
@export Is my claim an initial claim for benefits (s 6(1))?
GIVEN `my claim is made for the purpose of establishing my benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim made for the purpose of establishing your benefit period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my claim an initial claim for benefits` IF
    `s 6(1) initial claim for benefits` `my claim is made for the purpose of establishing my benefit period`

-- s 6(1) "major attachment claimant": a claimant who qualifies and has 600 or more hours of insurable employment in the qualifying period.
@export Am I a major attachment claimant (s 6(1))?
GIVEN `I qualify to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify to receive benefits (the answer to "Do I qualify for regular benefits")?
      `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a major attachment claimant` IF
    `s 6(1) major attachment claimant` `I qualify to receive benefits` `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period`

-- s 6(1) "minor attachment claimant": a claimant who qualifies and has fewer than 600 hours.
@export Am I a minor attachment claimant (s 6(1))?
GIVEN `I qualify to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify to receive benefits (the answer to "Do I qualify for regular benefits")?
      `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a minor attachment claimant` IF
    `s 6(1) minor attachment claimant` `I qualify to receive benefits` `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period`

-- s 6(4) and (5). A job is not suitable employment if it arises from a work stoppage due to a labour dispute; or it is in my
-- usual occupation at a lower rate or on worse conditions than the agreement between employers and employees (or, with none,
-- what good employers recognize); or it is not in my usual occupation at a lower rate or on worse conditions than I might
-- reasonably expect. After a reasonable interval the third limb stops applying if the job is no worse than that benchmark.
@export Is a job offered to me not suitable employment (s 6(4), (5))?
GIVEN `the job arises in consequence of a work stoppage attributable to a labour dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the job arise in consequence of a work stoppage attributable to a labour dispute?
      `the job is in my usual occupation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the job in your usual occupation?
      `there is an agreement between employers and employees that covers the job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an agreement between employers and employees that covers this kind of job?
      `the job pays a lower rate of earnings than that agreement provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the job pay a lower rate of earnings than that agreement provides?
      `the job is on conditions less favourable than that agreement provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the job on conditions less favourable than that agreement provides?
      `the job pays a lower rate of earnings than good employers recognize` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the job pay a lower rate of earnings than good employers recognize?
      `the job is on conditions less favourable than good employers recognize` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the job on conditions less favourable than good employers recognize?
      `the job pays a lower rate of earnings than I might reasonably expect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the job pay a lower rate of earnings than you might reasonably expect, given the conditions you usually obtained in your usual occupation?
      `the job is on conditions less favourable than I might reasonably expect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the job on conditions less favourable than you might reasonably expect, given the conditions you usually obtained in your usual occupation?
      `a reasonable interval has lapsed since I became unemployed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a reasonable interval lapsed since you became unemployed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a job offered to me not suitable employment` IF
    `s 6(4) employment is not suitable employment`
        (`s 6(4)(a) employment arises in consequence of a work stoppage attributable to a labour dispute` `the job arises in consequence of a work stoppage attributable to a labour dispute`)
        (`s 6(4)(b) employment in the claimant's usual occupation is at a lower rate or on less favourable conditions` `the job is in my usual occupation` `the job is below the benchmark`)
        (`s 6(4)(c) employment outside the claimant's usual occupation is at a lower rate or on less favourable conditions than the claimant might reasonably expect` (NOT (`the job is in my usual occupation`)) `the job pays a lower rate of earnings than I might reasonably expect` `the job is on conditions less favourable than I might reasonably expect`)
        (`s 6(5) paragraph 6(4)(c) does not apply after a reasonable interval` `a reasonable interval has lapsed since I became unemployed` (NOT (`the job is below the benchmark`)))
    WHERE
        `the job is below the benchmark` MEANS
            `s 6(4)(b) and s 6(5) at a lower rate of earnings or on conditions less favourable than the benchmark` `there is an agreement between employers and employees that covers the job` `the job pays a lower rate of earnings than that agreement provides` `the job is on conditions less favourable than that agreement provides` `the job pays a lower rate of earnings than good employers recognize` `the job is on conditions less favourable than good employers recognize`

§§ `Do I qualify, and how many hours do I need (sections 7 and 7.1)`

-- s 7(1): unemployment benefits are payable as provided in Part I to an insured person who qualifies to receive them.
@export Are unemployment benefits payable to me under Part I (s 7(1))?
GIVEN `I am an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or have you been, employed in insurable employment?
      `I qualify to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify to receive benefits (the answer to "Do I qualify for regular benefits")?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are unemployment benefits payable to me under Part I` IF
    `s 7(1) unemployment benefits are payable as provided in Part I to the insured person` `I am an insured person` `I qualify to receive benefits`

-- ss 7(1), 7(2), 7(6), 7.1(1), 7.1(3). I qualify if my earnings have been interrupted and I have enough hours of insurable employment in my
-- qualifying period for my regional rate of unemployment (or the higher figure if I have a violation from the last 260 weeks), unless
-- it is jointly determined under the Canada-U.S. agreement that I must first exhaust benefit rights there.
@export Do I qualify for regular benefits (ss 7, 7.1)?
GIVEN `I am an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, or have you been, employed in insurable employment?
      `my earnings from employment have been interrupted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has there been an interruption of your earnings from employment, as the Regulations define it?
      `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period?
      `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the regional rate of unemployment that applies to you, as a decimal fraction (6.5% is 0.065)?
      `I have a violation from the 260 weeks before my initial claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you accumulate a violation (a notice of violation from the Commission) in the 260 weeks before you make your initial claim? If you have more than one, answer for the one of the highest class.
      `the class of my violation` IS A `Violation class` @desc What is the class of your violation? One of: a minor violation, a serious violation, a very serious violation, a subsequent violation.
      `the day I accumulated my violation` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you accumulate your violation (the day the Commission issued the notice of violation), as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `the earlier initial claims in which my violation was counted and I qualified` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many earlier initial claims was your violation taken into account and did you qualify?
      `the day I make my initial claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make your initial claim for benefits, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `I must first exhaust or end benefit rights in the United States` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been jointly determined that you must first exhaust or end benefit rights under the laws of another jurisdiction, as provided by Article VI of the Canada-U.S. unemployment insurance agreement of 1942?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I qualify for regular benefits` IF
    `s 7 and s 7.1 the insured person qualifies to receive benefits` `I am an insured person` `my earnings from employment have been interrupted` `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period`
        (`s 7.1(1) the number of hours that an insured person requires` `the classes of my violations` `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me`)
        `I must first exhaust or end benefit rights in the United States`
    WHERE
        `my violations` MEANS
            IF `I have a violation from the 260 weeks before my initial claim`
            THEN LIST (`ei1 Violation` OF `the class of my violation`, `the day I accumulated my violation`, `the earlier initial claims in which my violation was counted and I qualified`)
            ELSE EMPTY
        `the classes of my violations` MEANS
            `s 7.1(1) the classes of the violations that raise the hours required` `my violations` `the day I make my initial claim`

@export How many hours of insurable employment do I need to qualify (ss 7(2), 7.1)?
GIVEN `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the regional rate of unemployment that applies to you, as a decimal fraction (6.5% is 0.065)?
      `I have a violation from the 260 weeks before my initial claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you accumulate a violation (a notice of violation from the Commission) in the 260 weeks before you make your initial claim? If you have more than one, answer for the one of the highest class.
      `the class of my violation` IS A `Violation class` @desc What is the class of your violation? One of: a minor violation, a serious violation, a very serious violation, a subsequent violation.
      `the day I accumulated my violation` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you accumulate your violation (the day the Commission issued the notice of violation), as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `the earlier initial claims in which my violation was counted and I qualified` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many earlier initial claims was your violation taken into account and did you qualify?
      `the day I make my initial claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make your initial claim for benefits, as YYYY-MM-DD?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours of insurable employment do I need to qualify for regular benefits` IS
    `s 7.1(1) the number of hours that an insured person requires` `the classes of my violations` `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me`
    WHERE
        `my violations` MEANS
            IF `I have a violation from the 260 weeks before my initial claim`
            THEN LIST (`ei1 Violation` OF `the class of my violation`, `the day I accumulated my violation`, `the earlier initial claims in which my violation was counted and I qualified`)
            ELSE EMPTY
        `the classes of my violations` MEANS
            `s 7.1(1) the classes of the violations that raise the hours required` `my violations` `the day I make my initial claim`

-- s 7(2) with no violation: the hours the table of section 7 requires for my regional rate.
@export How many hours do I need if I have no violation (s 7(2))?
GIVEN `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the regional rate of unemployment that applies to you, as a decimal fraction (6.5% is 0.065)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours of insurable employment do I need if I have no violation` IS
    `s 7(2)(b) the number of hours of insurable employment required in relation to the regional rate of unemployment` `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me`

-- s 7.1(3): a violation is taken into account in at most two initial claims in which the person qualified.
@export May my violation be counted again in this initial claim (s 7.1(3))?
GIVEN `the earlier initial claims in which my violation was counted and I qualified` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many earlier initial claims was your violation taken into account and did you qualify?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my violation be counted again in this initial claim` IF
    `s 7.1(3) the violation may be taken into account in this initial claim` `the earlier initial claims in which my violation was counted and I qualified`

-- s 7.1(1) and (2.1): the day a violation is accumulated, and whether it falls in the 260 weeks before the initial claim.
@export Did I accumulate my violation within the 260 weeks before my initial claim (s 7.1(1))?
GIVEN `the day I accumulated my violation` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you accumulate your violation (the day the Commission issued the notice of violation), as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `the day I make my initial claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make your initial claim for benefits, as YYYY-MM-DD?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I accumulate my violation within the 260 weeks before my initial claim` IF
    `s 7.1(1) the violation was accumulated in the 260 weeks before the initial claim` `the day I accumulated my violation` `the day I make my initial claim`

@export On what day is my self-employed violation treated as accumulated for regular benefits (s 7.1(2.1))?
GIVEN `the day the notice of violation was given to me under section 152.07` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice of violation given to you as a self-employed person under section 152.07, as YYYY-MM-DD?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day is my self-employed violation treated as accumulated for regular benefits` IS
    `s 7.1(2.1) the day on which a violation accumulated under section 152.07 is deemed to be accumulated under section 7.1` `the day the notice of violation was given to me under section 152.07`

-- s 7.1(4): I accumulate a violation if the Commission issues me a notice of violation in one of three circumstances.
@export Have I accumulated a violation (s 7.1(4))?
GIVEN `the Commission issued me a notice of violation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission issue you a notice of violation?
      `I was penalized under section 38, 39, 41.1 or 65.1 for acts or omissions mentioned in section 38, 39 or 65.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you penalized under section 38, 39, 41.1 or 65.1 of the Act for acts or omissions mentioned in section 38, 39 or 65.1?
      `I was found guilty of an offence under section 135 or 136 for acts or omissions mentioned in those sections` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found guilty of an offence under section 135 or 136 of the Act for acts or omissions mentioned in those sections?
      `I was found guilty of an offence under the Criminal Code for acts or omissions relating to the application of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found guilty of an offence under the Criminal Code for acts or omissions relating to the application of the Employment Insurance Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I accumulated a violation` IF
    `s 7.1(4) an insured person accumulates a violation` `the Commission issued me a notice of violation` `I was penalized under section 38, 39, 41.1 or 65.1 for acts or omissions mentioned in section 38, 39 or 65.1` `I was found guilty of an offence under section 135 or 136 for acts or omissions mentioned in those sections` `I was found guilty of an offence under the Criminal Code for acts or omissions relating to the application of the Act`

-- s 7.1(5)(b): a notice of violation issued within 260 weeks after I accumulated another violation makes it a subsequent violation. This question looks at up to two other violations.
@export Was my notice of violation issued within 260 weeks after I accumulated another violation (s 7.1(5)(b))?
GIVEN `the day the notice of violation is issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date is (or was) your notice of violation issued, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `I accumulated a first other violation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you accumulate another violation before this notice of violation?
      `the day I accumulated my first other violation` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you accumulate that other violation, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored if you had none.
      `I accumulated a second other violation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you accumulate a second other violation before this notice of violation?
      `the day I accumulated my second other violation` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you accumulate that second other violation, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored if you had none.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my notice of violation issued within 260 weeks after I accumulated another violation` IF
    `s 7.1(5)(b) the notice of violation is issued within 260 weeks after the person accumulates another violation` `the day the notice of violation is issued` (concat (LIST (IF `I accumulated a first other violation` THEN LIST `the day I accumulated my first other violation` ELSE EMPTY), (IF `I accumulated a second other violation` THEN LIST `the day I accumulated my second other violation` ELSE EMPTY)))

-- s 7.1(5): a violation for which only a warning was imposed has no class (the answer is then NOTHING). Otherwise it is subsequent if the
-- notice came within 260 weeks after another violation, and if not, minor (under $1,000), serious ($1,000 to under $5,000) or very serious ($5,000 or more).
@export What class is my violation (s 7.1(5))?
GIVEN `a warning was imposed for my violation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was only a warning imposed for the violation?
      `my notice of violation was issued within 260 weeks after I accumulated another violation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your notice of violation issued within 260 weeks after you accumulated another violation?
      `the value of my violation` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of your violation, in dollars (the overpayment plus any amount under section 7.1(6)(b))?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Violation class`
DECIDE `What class is my violation` IS
    `s 7.1(5) the class of the violation` `a warning was imposed for my violation` `my notice of violation was issued within 260 weeks after I accumulated another violation` `the value of my violation`

-- s 7.1(6) and (7): the value of a violation is the overpayment plus, if I am disqualified or disentitled or the acts relate to the
-- qualification requirements, my weekly rate times the average number of weeks of regular benefits, but not more than I could have been paid.
@export What is the value of my violation (s 7.1(6), (7))?
GIVEN `the overpayment of benefits resulting from the acts or omissions on which my violation is based` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the overpayment of benefits resulting from the acts or omissions on which your violation is based, in dollars?
      `I am disqualified or disentitled from receiving benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you disqualified or disentitled from receiving benefits?
      `the acts or omissions relate to the qualification requirements under section 7` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the acts or omissions on which your violation is based relate to the qualification requirements under section 7?
      `my weekly rate of benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your weekly rate of benefit, in dollars?
      `the average number of weeks of regular benefits under the regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the average number of weeks of regular benefits for your claim, as determined under the Regulations (reg 13)?
      `the amount of benefits that could have been paid to me` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of benefits that could have been paid to you had you not been disentitled or disqualified, or had you met the qualification requirements under section 7, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the value of my violation` IS
    `s 7.1(6) the value of the violation` `the overpayment of benefits resulting from the acts or omissions on which my violation is based` `I am disqualified or disentitled from receiving benefits` `the acts or omissions relate to the qualification requirements under section 7` (`s 7.1(7) the amount determined under paragraph 7.1(6)(b)` `my weekly rate of benefit` `the average number of weeks of regular benefits under the regulations` `the amount of benefits that could have been paid to me`)

§§ `My qualifying period (section 8)`

-- Section 8: the period in which my hours of insurable employment are counted.

-- s 8(1): the qualifying period is the shorter of the 52 weeks before my benefit period and the period since an immediately preceding benefit period began;
-- only the 52-week period is extended (s 8(2), (4)) by weeks I prove I was not employed in insurable employment for certain reasons, to at most 104 weeks.
@export On what date does my qualifying period begin (s 8)?
GIVEN `the day my benefit period begins` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your benefit period begin (a Sunday), as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `I had an immediately preceding benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have an immediately preceding benefit period?
      `my immediately preceding benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your immediately preceding benefit period begin (a Sunday), as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored if you had none.
      `the weeks in my 52 weeks that extend my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks in your qualifying period do you prove you were not employed in insurable employment because you were incapable of work (prescribed illness, injury, quarantine or pregnancy), confined in a jail and not found guilty, receiving assistance under an employment support measure, or receiving provincial-law payments because continuing to work was dangerous, not counting weeks in which you received benefits?
      `the weeks in an extension that further extend my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks during an extension of your qualifying period do you prove you were not employed in insurable employment for one of those reasons, not counting weeks in which you received benefits?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my qualifying period begin` IS
    (`s 8 the qualifying period` `the day my benefit period begins` `my immediately preceding benefit period, if any` `the weeks in my 52 weeks that extend my qualifying period` `the weeks in an extension that further extend my qualifying period`)'s `first day of the period`
    WHERE
        `my immediately preceding benefit period, if any` MEANS
            IF `I had an immediately preceding benefit period` THEN JUST `my immediately preceding benefit period began on` ELSE NOTHING

@export On what date does my qualifying period end (s 8)?
GIVEN `the day my benefit period begins` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your benefit period begin (a Sunday), as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `I had an immediately preceding benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have an immediately preceding benefit period?
      `my immediately preceding benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your immediately preceding benefit period begin (a Sunday), as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored if you had none.
      `the weeks in my 52 weeks that extend my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks in your qualifying period do you prove you were not employed in insurable employment because you were incapable of work (prescribed illness, injury, quarantine or pregnancy), confined in a jail and not found guilty, receiving assistance under an employment support measure, or receiving provincial-law payments because continuing to work was dangerous, not counting weeks in which you received benefits?
      `the weeks in an extension that further extend my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks during an extension of your qualifying period do you prove you were not employed in insurable employment for one of those reasons, not counting weeks in which you received benefits?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my qualifying period end` IS
    (`s 8 the qualifying period` `the day my benefit period begins` `my immediately preceding benefit period, if any` `the weeks in my 52 weeks that extend my qualifying period` `the weeks in an extension that further extend my qualifying period`)'s `last day of the period`
    WHERE
        `my immediately preceding benefit period, if any` MEANS
            IF `I had an immediately preceding benefit period` THEN JUST `my immediately preceding benefit period began on` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 8(2), (4), (5): a week extends my qualifying period if I prove I was not employed in insurable employment throughout it because I was
-- incapable of work (prescribed illness, injury, quarantine, pregnancy), held in a jail and not found guilty, receiving assistance under an
-- employment support measure (other than one in 59(c) or (d)), or receiving provincial-law payments for danger; a week in which I received benefits does not count.
@export Does this week extend my qualifying period (s 8(2), (4), (5))?
GIVEN `I prove, in the manner the Commission directs, that I was not employed in insurable employment throughout the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you prove, in the manner the Commission directs, that throughout the week you were not employed in insurable employment?
      `I was incapable of work because of a prescribed illness, injury, quarantine or pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you incapable of work that week because of a prescribed illness, injury, quarantine or pregnancy?
      `I was confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you confined that week in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution?
      `I was found guilty of the offence for which I was held or another offence from the same transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found guilty of the offence for which you were held, or any other offence arising out of the same transaction?
      `I was receiving assistance under an employment support measure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you receiving assistance that week under an employment support measure?
      `that employment support measure is one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that measure one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d) of the Act?
      `I was receiving payments under a provincial law because continuing to work would have endangered me or my child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you receiving payments under a provincial law because you ceased to work, as continuing to work would have been dangerous to you, your unborn child or a child you were breast-feeding?
      `the week falls during an extension of my qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the week fall during an extension of your qualifying period (rather than in the 52 weeks before your benefit period)?
      `I received benefits during the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive benefits during that week?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this week extend my qualifying period` IF
    `s 8(5) the week counts for the purposes of subsections 8(2) and 8(4)` `I received benefits during the week`
    AND (IF `the week falls during an extension of my qualifying period`
         THEN `s 8(4) the week during an extension further extends the qualifying period` `the week falls during an extension of my qualifying period` `the week is a reason week`
         ELSE `the week is a reason week`)
    WHERE
        `the week is a reason week` MEANS
            `s 8(2) the week is one for which the person was not employed in insurable employment for a reason that extends the qualifying period` `I prove, in the manner the Commission directs, that I was not employed in insurable employment throughout the week` `I was incapable of work because of a prescribed illness, injury, quarantine or pregnancy` `I was confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution` `I was found guilty of the offence for which I was held or another offence from the same transaction` `I was receiving assistance under an employment support measure` `that employment support measure is one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d)` `I was receiving payments under a provincial law because continuing to work would have endangered me or my child`

§§ `My benefit period (sections 9 and 10)`

-- Section 9: a benefit period is established when an insured person who qualifies makes an initial claim; section 10: when it begins, how long it is, late claims, cancelling, ending and extending it.

-- ss 9 and 10(3): a benefit period is established when I qualify and make an initial claim, unless a prior benefit period of mine has not ended.
@export Will a benefit period be established for me (ss 9, 10(3))?
GIVEN `I qualify to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify to receive benefits (the answer to "Do I qualify for regular benefits")?
      `I make an initial claim for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make an initial claim for benefits (a claim made to establish your benefit period)?
      `a prior benefit period of mine has not ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a prior benefit period of yours that has not ended?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will a benefit period be established for me` IF
    `s 9 and s 10(3) a benefit period is established for the claimant` (`s 9 a benefit period shall be established` `I qualify to receive benefits` `I make an initial claim for benefits`) (`s 10(3) a benefit period shall not be established for the claimant` `a prior benefit period of mine has not ended`)

-- s 9: once a benefit period is established, benefits are payable for each week of unemployment that falls in it.
@export Are benefits payable to me for this week of unemployment (s 9)?
GIVEN `a benefit period has been established for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a benefit period been established for you?
      `the week is a week of unemployment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the week a week of unemployment for you (see "Is this week a week of unemployment for me")?
      `the week falls in my benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the week fall in your benefit period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are benefits payable to me for this week of unemployment` IF
    `s 9 benefits are payable to the person in accordance with Part I for the week` `a benefit period has been established for me` (`the week is a week of unemployment` AND `the week falls in my benefit period`)

-- s 10(1): the benefit period begins on the later of the Sunday of the week in which my earnings were interrupted and the Sunday of the week in which I make my initial claim.
@export On what date does my benefit period begin (s 10(1))?
GIVEN `the day my earnings were interrupted` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the interruption of your earnings occur, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `the day I make my initial claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make your initial claim for benefits, as YYYY-MM-DD?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my benefit period begin` IS
    `s 10(1) the first day of the benefit period` `the day my earnings were interrupted` `the day I make my initial claim`

-- s 10(4): a late initial claim is treated as made on an earlier day if I show I qualified on that day and had good cause for the delay throughout.
@export Is my late initial claim treated as made on an earlier date (s 10(4))?
GIVEN `the day I make my initial claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make your initial claim for benefits, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `the day I was first qualified to make the claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you first qualified to make the claim, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `the earlier day on which I ask for the claim to be treated as made` IS A DATE @desc What earlier date do you ask the claim to be treated as made on, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `I show that I qualified to receive benefits on the earlier day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you show that you qualified to receive benefits on that earlier day?
      `I show good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day to the day I made the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you show that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day to the day you made the claim?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my late initial claim treated as made on an earlier date` IF
    `s 10(4) the initial claim for benefits is regarded as having been made on the earlier day` `the day I make my initial claim` `the day I was first qualified to make the claim` `the earlier day on which I ask for the claim to be treated as made` `I show that I qualified to receive benefits on the earlier day` `I show good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day to the day I made the claim`

-- s 10(4), (5) and (5.1) to (5.3): a late claim is treated as made earlier if I show good cause throughout (and, for an initial claim, that I qualified);
-- but a late claim for compassionate care, a critically ill child or a critically ill adult is not so treated if benefits are exhausted, the period
-- is already fixed and the claim would move it earlier, or the regulations set out other circumstances.
@export Is my late claim treated as made on an earlier date (s 10(4), (5), (5.1) to (5.3))?
GIVEN `my claim is an initial claim for benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim an initial claim for benefits (a claim made to establish your benefit period)?
      `the day I made my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the claim, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `the day I was first qualified to make the claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date were you first qualified to make the claim, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `the last day of the time prescribed for making my claim` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the time prescribed for making your claim (see regulation 26), as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored for an initial claim.
      `the earlier day on which I ask for the claim to be treated as made` IS A DATE @desc What earlier date do you ask the claim to be treated as made on, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `I show that I qualified to receive benefits on the earlier day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you show that you qualified to receive benefits on that earlier day?
      `I show good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day to the day I made the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you show that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day to the day you made the claim?
      `my claim is for compassionate care benefits under section 23.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim a claim for compassionate care benefits under section 23.1?
      `my claim is for benefits for a critically ill child under section 23.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim a claim for benefits for a critically ill child under section 23.2?
      `my claim is for benefits for a critically ill adult under section 23.3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim a claim for benefits for a critically ill adult under section 23.3?
      `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time the claim is made, have all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to it already been exhausted?
      `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the beginning of the period during which benefits are payable for the person you care for already been determined?
      `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your claim have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date?
      `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my late claim treated as made on an earlier date` IF
    BRANCH IF `my claim is for compassionate care benefits under section 23.1` THEN `s 10(5.1) a claim for benefits referred to in section 23.1 is regarded as having been made on an earlier day` `the claim as it would be without the exception` `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`
           IF `my claim is for benefits for a critically ill child under section 23.2` THEN `s 10(5.2) a claim for benefits referred to in section 23.2 is regarded as having been made on an earlier day` `the claim as it would be without the exception` `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`
           IF `my claim is for benefits for a critically ill adult under section 23.3` THEN `s 10(5.3) a claim for benefits referred to in section 23.3 is regarded as having been made on an earlier day` `the claim as it would be without the exception` `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`
           OTHERWISE `the claim as it would be without the exception`
    WHERE
        `the claim as it would be without the exception` MEANS
            IF `my claim is an initial claim for benefits`
            THEN `s 10(4) the initial claim for benefits is regarded as having been made on the earlier day` `the day I made my claim` `the day I was first qualified to make the claim` `the earlier day on which I ask for the claim to be treated as made` `I show that I qualified to receive benefits on the earlier day` `I show good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day to the day I made the claim`
            ELSE `s 10(5) the claim for benefits other than an initial claim is regarded as having been made on the earlier day` `the day I made my claim` `the last day of the time prescribed for making my claim` `the earlier day on which I ask for the claim to be treated as made` `I show good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day to the day I made the claim`

-- s 10(6): the Commission may cancel my benefit period if it has ended and nothing was paid or payable; or, at my request, the part before the first week
-- for which benefits were paid or payable, if I establish a new benefit period from that week and show good cause for the delay in asking.
@export May the Commission cancel my benefit period or part of it (s 10(6))?
GIVEN `my benefit period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your benefit period ended?
      `no benefits were paid or payable during my benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were no benefits paid or payable during your benefit period?
      `I ask for the cancellation of the part of my benefit period before the first week for which benefits were paid or payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you ask for the cancellation of the part of your benefit period immediately before the first week for which benefits were paid or payable?
      `I establish a new benefit period as an insured person beginning the first week for which benefits were paid or payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you establish a new benefit period, as an insured person under Part I, beginning the first week for which benefits were paid or payable?
      `I establish a new benefit period as a self-employed person beginning the first week for which benefits were paid or payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you establish a new benefit period, as a self-employed person under Part VII.1, beginning the first week for which benefits were paid or payable?
      `I show good cause for the delay in asking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you show that there was good cause for the delay in making the request, throughout the period from the day benefits were first paid or payable to the day you made the request?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission cancel my benefit period or part of it` IF
    `s 10(6)(a) the Commission may cancel the benefit period` `my benefit period has ended` `no benefits were paid or payable during my benefit period`
    OR `s 10(6)(b) the Commission may cancel at the request of the claimant the portion of the benefit period immediately before the first week for which benefits were paid or payable` `I ask for the cancellation of the part of my benefit period before the first week for which benefits were paid or payable` `I establish a new benefit period as an insured person beginning the first week for which benefits were paid or payable` `I establish a new benefit period as a self-employed person beginning the first week for which benefits were paid or payable` `I show good cause for the delay in asking`

-- s 10(7): a cancelled benefit period or part of it is treated as never having begun.
@export Is my cancelled benefit period treated as never having begun (s 10(7))?
GIVEN `my benefit period or part of it has been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your benefit period, or part of it, been cancelled?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my cancelled benefit period treated as never having begun` IF
    `s 10(7) the cancelled benefit period or portion of a benefit period is deemed never to have begun` `my benefit period or part of it has been cancelled`

-- s 10(8): my benefit period ends on the earliest of the day no further benefits are payable, the day it would otherwise end under section 10, and the day I have
-- requested it to end, made a new initial claim and qualified on it.
@export On what date does my benefit period end (s 10(8))?
GIVEN `no further benefits are payable to me in my benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have no further benefits become payable to you in your benefit period (for example because benefits were paid for the maximum number of weeks under section 12)?
      `the day on which no further benefits are payable to me` IS A DATE @desc On what date did no further benefits become payable to you, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored if they have not.
      `the day my benefit period would otherwise end` IS A DATE @desc On what date would your benefit period otherwise end under section 10 (the last day of its length), as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `I have requested that my benefit period end` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you requested that your benefit period end?
      `the day I requested that my benefit period end` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you request that your benefit period end, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored if you have not.
      `I have made a new initial claim under Part I or Part VII.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a new initial claim for benefits under Part I or Part VII.1?
      `the day I made the new initial claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the new initial claim, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored if you have not.
      `I qualify, as an insured person or as a self-employed person, to receive benefits on the new claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify, as an insured person under Part I or as a self-employed person under Part VII.1, to receive benefits on the new claim?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my benefit period end` IS
    `s 10(8) the day on which the benefit period ends` (IF `no further benefits are payable to me in my benefit period` THEN JUST `the day on which no further benefits are payable to me` ELSE NOTHING) `the day my benefit period would otherwise end` (`s 10(8)(d) the day on which the claimant requests the end of the benefit period, makes a new initial claim and qualifies` (IF `I have requested that my benefit period end` THEN JUST `the day I requested that my benefit period end` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `I have made a new initial claim under Part I or Part VII.1` THEN JUST `the day I made the new initial claim` ELSE NOTHING) `I qualify, as an insured person or as a self-employed person, to receive benefits on the new claim`)

-- s 10(9): a late request that my benefit period end is treated as made on an earlier day if I show good cause for the delay throughout.
@export Is my late request that my benefit period end treated as made earlier (s 10(9))?
GIVEN `the day I made my request that my benefit period end` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make your request that your benefit period end, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `the earlier day on which I ask for the claim to be treated as made` IS A DATE @desc What earlier date do you ask the claim to be treated as made on, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `I show good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day to the day I made the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you show that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day to the day you made the request?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my late request that my benefit period end treated as made earlier` IF
    `s 10(9) the request under paragraph 10(8)(d) is regarded as having been made on the earlier day` `the day I made my request that my benefit period end` `the earlier day on which I ask for the claim to be treated as made` `I show good cause for the delay throughout the period from the earlier day to the day I made the request`

-- s 10(10) and (11): a week extends my benefit period if I prove I was not entitled to benefits that week because I was held in a jail and not found guilty, was paid
-- severe earnings, was paid workers' compensation, or was paid provincial-law payments because continuing to work was dangerous; (11) the same for a week in an extension.
@export Does this week extend my benefit period (s 10(10), (11))?
GIVEN `I prove, in the manner the Commission directs, that I was not entitled to benefits in the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you prove, in the manner the Commission directs, that you were not entitled to benefits in the week?
      `I was confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you confined that week in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution?
      `I was found guilty of the offence for which I was held or another offence from the same transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you found guilty of the offence for which you were held, or any other offence arising out of the same transaction?
      `I was in receipt of earnings paid because of the complete severance of my relationship with my former employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in receipt of earnings paid because of the complete severance of your relationship with your former employer?
      `I was in receipt of workers' compensation payments for an illness or injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in receipt of workers' compensation payments for an illness or injury?
      `I was in receipt of payments under a provincial law because continuing to work would have endangered me or my child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you in receipt of payments under a provincial law because you ceased to work, as continuing to work would have been dangerous to you, your unborn child or a child you were breast-feeding?
      `the week falls during an extension of my benefit period under section 10(10)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the week fall during an extension of your benefit period (rather than in the benefit period itself)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this week extend my benefit period` IF
    IF `the week falls during an extension of my benefit period under section 10(10)`
    THEN `s 10(11) the week during an extension further extends the benefit period` `the week falls during an extension of my benefit period under section 10(10)` `the week is a reason week`
    ELSE `the week is a reason week`
    WHERE
        `the week is a reason week` MEANS
            `s 10(10) the week is one for which the claimant was not entitled to benefits for a reason that extends the benefit period` `I prove, in the manner the Commission directs, that I was not entitled to benefits in the week` `I was confined in a jail, penitentiary or other similar institution` `I was found guilty of the offence for which I was held or another offence from the same transaction` `I was in receipt of earnings paid because of the complete severance of my relationship with my former employer` `I was in receipt of workers' compensation payments for an illness or injury` `I was in receipt of payments under a provincial law because continuing to work would have endangered me or my child`

-- ss 10(2) and (10) to (15): a benefit period is 52 weeks, plus the weeks of the extensions, but at most 104 weeks, plus any extension made by work-sharing regulations under section 24.
@export How many weeks long is my benefit period (s 10(2), (10) to (15))?
GIVEN `the weeks in my benefit period for which I was not entitled to benefits for a reason that extends it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks in your benefit period do you prove you were not entitled to benefits because you were held in a jail and not found guilty, were paid severance earnings, were paid workers' compensation, or were paid provincial-law payments because continuing to work was dangerous?
      `the weeks in an extension for which I was not entitled to benefits for one of those reasons` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks during such an extension of your benefit period do you prove you were not entitled to benefits for one of those reasons?
      `my child was in hospital during the period for parental benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your child, or were your children, in hospital during the period during which parental benefits are payable?
      `the weeks my child was in hospital` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks was your child, or were your children, in hospital? Ignored if not in hospital.
      `my parental leave was deferred or I was directed to return to duty under the National Defence Act regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period during which parental benefits are payable, was the start of your parental leave deferred, or were you directed to return to duty from parental leave, under regulations made under the National Defence Act?
      `the weeks my parental leave was deferred or I was directed to return to duty` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks was your parental leave deferred or were you directed to return to duty? Ignored if not.
      `I was paid regular benefits in my benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you paid regular benefits during your benefit period?
      `the weeks of maternity benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits because of pregnancy in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of parental benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits for caring for a new-born or adopted child in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of sickness benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of compassionate care benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits for the care or support of a family member in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill child I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits for the care or support of a critically ill child in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill adult I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits for the care or support of a critically ill adult in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `my election of the maximum number of weeks` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks` @desc Which maximum number of weeks did you elect for caring for a new-born or adopted child? One of: the 35-week maximum, the 61-week maximum.
      `I was paid benefits for fewer than the total number of weeks established under section 12(6) as determined under section 12(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you paid benefits for fewer than the total number of weeks established under subsection 12(6), as determined under subsection 12(7)?
      `the weeks by which my benefit period must be extended to reach that total` IS A NUMBER @desc By how many weeks must your benefit period be extended so that benefits may be paid up to that total number of weeks (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of extension under regulations made under section 24` IS A NUMBER @desc By how many weeks do regulations made under paragraph 24(1)(g) (work-sharing) extend your benefit period (0 if none)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks long is my benefit period` IS
    `s 10(2) and s 10(14) the length of the benefit period in weeks`
        (`s 10(10) and s 10(11) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` `the weeks in my benefit period for which I was not entitled to benefits for a reason that extends it` `the weeks in an extension for which I was not entitled to benefits for one of those reasons`)
        (`s 10(12) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended because the children are in hospital` `my child was in hospital during the period for parental benefits` `the weeks my child was in hospital`)
        (`s 10(12.1) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended because of the Canadian Forces` `my parental leave was deferred or I was directed to return to duty under the National Defence Act regulations` `the weeks my parental leave was deferred or I was directed to return to duty`)
        (`s 10(13) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` `I was paid regular benefits in my benefit period` `the special benefits I was paid` `my election of the maximum number of weeks`)
        (`s 10(13.01) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)` `parental benefits were paid` `my election of the maximum number of weeks` `I was paid regular benefits in my benefit period` `other special benefits were paid`)
        (`s 10(13.02) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended for regular and special benefits` `I was paid regular benefits in my benefit period` `parental benefits were paid` `my election of the maximum number of weeks` `I was paid benefits for fewer than the total number of weeks established under section 12(6) as determined under section 12(7)` `the weeks by which my benefit period must be extended to reach that total`)
        `the weeks of extension under regulations made under section 24`
    WHERE
        `the special benefits I was paid` MEANS
            LIST (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `pregnancy`, `the weeks of maternity benefits I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `caring for a new-born or adopted child`, `the weeks of parental benefits I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine`, `the weeks of sickness benefits I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `care or support of a family member`, `the weeks of compassionate care benefits I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `care or support of a critically ill child`, `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill child I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `care or support of a critically ill adult`, `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill adult I was paid`)
        `parental benefits were paid` MEANS `the weeks of parental benefits I was paid` GREATER THAN 0
        `other special benefits were paid` MEANS
               `the weeks of maternity benefits I was paid` GREATER THAN 0
            OR `the weeks of sickness benefits I was paid` GREATER THAN 0
            OR `the weeks of compassionate care benefits I was paid` GREATER THAN 0
            OR `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill child I was paid` GREATER THAN 0
            OR `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill adult I was paid` GREATER THAN 0

-- s 10(13): the benefit period is extended so special benefits can be paid up to the maximum total weeks when I was paid no regular benefits, was paid for more than one
-- special reason and not for the full maximum of one of them, and the maximum total is more than 50 weeks.
@export Is my benefit period extended so that I can be paid special benefits up to the maximum (s 10(13))?
GIVEN `I was paid regular benefits in my benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you paid regular benefits during your benefit period?
      `the weeks of maternity benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits because of pregnancy in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of parental benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits for caring for a new-born or adopted child in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of sickness benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of compassionate care benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits for the care or support of a family member in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill child I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits for the care or support of a critically ill child in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill adult I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits for the care or support of a critically ill adult in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `my election of the maximum number of weeks` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks` @desc Which maximum number of weeks did you elect for caring for a new-born or adopted child? One of: the 35-week maximum, the 61-week maximum.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my benefit period extended so that I can be paid special benefits up to the maximum` IF
    `s 10(13) the benefit period is extended so that special benefits may be paid up to the maximum total number of weeks` `I was paid regular benefits in my benefit period` `the special benefits I was paid` `my election of the maximum number of weeks`
    WHERE
        `the special benefits I was paid` MEANS
            LIST (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `pregnancy`, `the weeks of maternity benefits I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `caring for a new-born or adopted child`, `the weeks of parental benefits I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine`, `the weeks of sickness benefits I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `care or support of a family member`, `the weeks of compassionate care benefits I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `care or support of a critically ill child`, `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill child I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `care or support of a critically ill adult`, `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill adult I was paid`)

-- s 10(15): the longest the benefit period can be when extended for special benefits: 2 weeks more than the total of the maxima of the special benefits paid, and at most 104 weeks.
@export What is the longest my benefit period can be after an extension for special benefits (s 10(15))?
GIVEN `the weeks of maternity benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits because of pregnancy in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of parental benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits for caring for a new-born or adopted child in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of sickness benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of compassionate care benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits for the care or support of a family member in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill child I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits for the care or support of a critically ill child in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill adult I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits for the care or support of a critically ill adult in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `my election of the maximum number of weeks` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks` @desc Which maximum number of weeks did you elect for caring for a new-born or adopted child? One of: the 35-week maximum, the 61-week maximum.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest my benefit period can be after an extension for special benefits` IS
    `s 10(15) the maximum number of weeks in a benefit period extended under subsection (13)` `the special benefits I was paid` `my election of the maximum number of weeks`
    WHERE
        `the special benefits I was paid` MEANS
            LIST (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `pregnancy`, `the weeks of maternity benefits I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `caring for a new-born or adopted child`, `the weeks of parental benefits I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine`, `the weeks of sickness benefits I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `care or support of a family member`, `the weeks of compassionate care benefits I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `care or support of a critically ill child`, `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill child I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `care or support of a critically ill adult`, `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill adult I was paid`)

-- s 10(13.03): during the extension of s 10(13.02) only the kinds of benefits already paid in the benefit period are payable.
@export Are benefits of this kind payable during the extension for regular and special benefits (s 10(13.03))?
GIVEN `benefits of that kind were paid in my benefit period before it was extended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were benefits of that kind (regular benefits, or benefits for one of the reasons in paragraphs 12(3)(a) to (f)) paid in your benefit period before it was extended under subsection 10(13.02)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are benefits of this kind payable during the extension for regular and special benefits` IF
    `s 10(13.03) benefits of that kind are payable during the extension under subsection (13.02)` `benefits of that kind were paid in my benefit period before it was extended`

§§ `Weeks of unemployment (section 11)`

-- s 11: a week of unemployment is a week in which I do not work a full working week, except a week on full pay, a week of leave with deferred pay, and counting a compensatory-leave week as worked.
@export Is this week a week of unemployment for me (s 11)?
GIVEN `I work a full working week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work a full working week in the week (as the Regulations define a full working week)?
      `my contract of service continues during the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your contract of service continue during the week?
      `I receive or will receive my usual remuneration for a full working week for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive, or will you receive, your usual remuneration for a full working week in respect of the week, even though you are excused from your normal duties or have none to perform?
      `the week is during a period of leave from employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the week, or part of it, in a period of leave from employment?
      `I take the leave under an agreement with my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you take the leave under an agreement with your employer?
      `I continue to be an employee of my employer during the leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you continue to be an employee of your employer during the leave?
      `I receive remuneration that was set aside during a period of work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive remuneration that was set aside during a period of work, whenever it is paid?
      `in each week I regularly work more hours, days or shifts than full-time employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In each week do you regularly work a greater number of hours, days or shifts than are normally worked in a week by persons employed in full-time employment?
      `I am entitled to the leave under an employment agreement to compensate for the extra time worked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to the period of leave under an employment agreement to compensate for the extra time you worked?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this week a week of unemployment for me` IF
    `s 11 a week of unemployment for a claimant` `I work a full working week` (`s 11(4) the insured person is deemed to have worked a full working week` `the week is during a period of leave from employment` `in each week I regularly work more hours, days or shifts than full-time employees` `I am entitled to the leave under an employment agreement to compensate for the extra time worked`) (`s 11(2) the week is not a week of unemployment although the claimant is excused from their normal duties` `my contract of service continues during the week` `I receive or will receive my usual remuneration for a full working week for the week`) (`s 11(3) the week or part of a week during a period of leave is not a week of unemployment` `the week is during a period of leave from employment` `I take the leave under an agreement with my employer` `I continue to be an employee of my employer during the leave` `I receive remuneration that was set aside during a period of work`)

§§ `How many weeks I can be paid (section 12)`

-- Section 12: the maximum weeks of benefits for each reason, and how weeks combine.

-- s 12(1): once a benefit period is established, benefits may be paid for each week of unemployment that falls in it, subject to the maximums of section 12.
@export May benefits be paid to me for this week (s 12(1))?
GIVEN `a benefit period has been established for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a benefit period been established for you?
      `the week is a week of unemployment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the week a week of unemployment for you (see "Is this week a week of unemployment for me")?
      `the week falls in my benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the week fall in your benefit period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May benefits be paid to me for this week` IF
    `s 12(1) benefits may be paid to the claimant for the week` `a benefit period has been established for me` `the week is a week of unemployment` `the week falls in my benefit period`

-- ss 12(2), (2.1), (2.3): the maximum weeks of regular benefits come from Schedule I, or 50 for benefit periods beginning from 27 September 2020 to 25 September 2021,
-- or from Schedule V for a seasonal worker in a Schedule VI region with at least three benefit periods in the last 260 weeks, two of them around the same time of year.
@export What is the most number of weeks of regular benefits I can be paid (s 12(2), (2.1), (2.3))?
GIVEN `the maximum number of weeks in the table in Schedule I for my regional rate and hours` IS A NUMBER @desc Looking up Schedule I of the Act with your regional rate of unemployment and your hours of insurable employment in your qualifying period, how many weeks does the table give?
      `the maximum number of weeks in the table in Schedule V for my regional rate and hours` IS A NUMBER @desc Looking up Schedule V of the Act with your regional rate of unemployment and your hours of insurable employment in your qualifying period, how many weeks does the table give (0 if it does not give one)?
      `the day my benefit period begins` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your benefit period begin (a Sunday), as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `I am a claimant under the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a claimant under the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations?
      `the day my benefit period is established` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your benefit period established, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `on that date I am ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule VI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On the date your benefit period is established, are you ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule VI of the Act?
      `I had a 1st earlier benefit period in which regular benefits were paid or payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a 1st earlier benefit period in the 260 weeks (or established before them) in which regular benefits were paid or payable? Answer no for any you did not have.
      `the 1st earlier benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that 1st earlier benefit period begin (a Sunday), as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored if you had none.
      `I had a 2nd earlier benefit period in which regular benefits were paid or payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a 2nd earlier benefit period in the 260 weeks (or established before them) in which regular benefits were paid or payable? Answer no for any you did not have.
      `the 2nd earlier benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that 2nd earlier benefit period begin (a Sunday), as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored if you had none.
      `I had a 3rd earlier benefit period in which regular benefits were paid or payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a 3rd earlier benefit period in the 260 weeks (or established before them) in which regular benefits were paid or payable? Answer no for any you did not have.
      `the 3rd earlier benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that 3rd earlier benefit period begin (a Sunday), as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored if you had none.
      `I had a 4th earlier benefit period in which regular benefits were paid or payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a 4th earlier benefit period in the 260 weeks (or established before them) in which regular benefits were paid or payable? Answer no for any you did not have.
      `the 4th earlier benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that 4th earlier benefit period begin (a Sunday), as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored if you had none.
      `I had a 5th earlier benefit period in which regular benefits were paid or payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a 5th earlier benefit period in the 260 weeks (or established before them) in which regular benefits were paid or payable? Answer no for any you did not have.
      `the 5th earlier benefit period began on` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that 5th earlier benefit period begin (a Sunday), as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored if you had none.
      `I was notified of payment or non-payment for a week within the 260 weeks before my benefit period began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you notified of payment or non-payment for a week that falls within the 260 weeks before your benefit period began? (This matters only for an earlier benefit period established before those 260 weeks.)
      `I met the criteria of regulation 77.992(2)(b) to (d) in an earlier benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you meet the criteria in paragraphs 77.992(2)(b) to (d) of the Employment Insurance Regulations, taking into account subsections 77.992(3) and (4), for a benefit period established within the period in paragraph 77.992(2)(a)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most number of weeks of regular benefits I can be paid` IS
    `s 12(2), s 12(2.1) and s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks for a reason other than those mentioned in subsection (3)`
        `the maximum number of weeks in the table in Schedule I for my regional rate and hours`
        `the maximum number of weeks in the table in Schedule V for my regional rate and hours`
        (`s 12(2.1) the maximum number of weeks is 50 for a benefit period that begins during the period` `the day my benefit period begins` `I am a claimant under the Employment Insurance (Fishing) Regulations`)
        (`s 12(2.3) the maximum number of weeks is read from the table in Schedule V` `the day my benefit period is established` `the day my benefit period begins` `on that date I am ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule VI` `my earlier benefit periods` `I met the criteria of regulation 77.992(2)(b) to (d) in an earlier benefit period`)
    WHERE
        `my earlier benefit periods` MEANS
            concat (LIST `my 1st earlier benefit period, if I had one`, `my 2nd earlier benefit period, if I had one`, `my 3rd earlier benefit period, if I had one`, `my 4th earlier benefit period, if I had one`, `my 5th earlier benefit period, if I had one`)
        `my 1st earlier benefit period, if I had one` MEANS
            IF `I had a 1st earlier benefit period in which regular benefits were paid or payable`
            THEN LIST (`ei1 Earlier benefit period` OF `the 1st earlier benefit period began on`, TRUE, `I was notified of payment or non-payment for a week within the 260 weeks before my benefit period began`)
            ELSE EMPTY
        `my 2nd earlier benefit period, if I had one` MEANS
            IF `I had a 2nd earlier benefit period in which regular benefits were paid or payable`
            THEN LIST (`ei1 Earlier benefit period` OF `the 2nd earlier benefit period began on`, TRUE, `I was notified of payment or non-payment for a week within the 260 weeks before my benefit period began`)
            ELSE EMPTY
        `my 3rd earlier benefit period, if I had one` MEANS
            IF `I had a 3rd earlier benefit period in which regular benefits were paid or payable`
            THEN LIST (`ei1 Earlier benefit period` OF `the 3rd earlier benefit period began on`, TRUE, `I was notified of payment or non-payment for a week within the 260 weeks before my benefit period began`)
            ELSE EMPTY
        `my 4th earlier benefit period, if I had one` MEANS
            IF `I had a 4th earlier benefit period in which regular benefits were paid or payable`
            THEN LIST (`ei1 Earlier benefit period` OF `the 4th earlier benefit period began on`, TRUE, `I was notified of payment or non-payment for a week within the 260 weeks before my benefit period began`)
            ELSE EMPTY
        `my 5th earlier benefit period, if I had one` MEANS
            IF `I had a 5th earlier benefit period in which regular benefits were paid or payable`
            THEN LIST (`ei1 Earlier benefit period` OF `the 5th earlier benefit period began on`, TRUE, `I was notified of payment or non-payment for a week within the 260 weeks before my benefit period began`)
            ELSE EMPTY

-- s 12(3): the maximum weeks in a benefit period for each special reason (NOTHING for a regular benefit, whose maximum is that of s 12(2)).
@export What is the most number of weeks of benefits for my reason (s 12(3))?
GIVEN `the reason I claim benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits` @desc For what reason do you claim benefits? One of: a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3), pregnancy, caring for a new-born or adopted child, a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine, care or support of a family member, care or support of a critically ill child, care or support of a critically ill adult.
      `my election of the maximum number of weeks` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks` @desc Which maximum number of weeks did you elect for caring for a new-born or adopted child? One of: the 35-week maximum, the 61-week maximum.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most number of weeks of benefits for my reason` IS
    `s 12(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period for the reason` `the reason I claim benefits` `my election of the maximum number of weeks`

-- s 12(4)(a): the maximum weeks of benefits for a single pregnancy.
@export How many weeks of benefits can I be paid for a single pregnancy (s 12(4)(a))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits can I be paid for a single pregnancy` IS
    `s 12(4)(a) the maximum number of weeks for a single pregnancy`

-- s 12(4)(b): the maximum weeks for the care of new-born or adopted children from one pregnancy or placement: 35, or 40 if divided under section 23; 61, or 69 if divided.
@export How many weeks can be paid for the care of my new-born or adopted child (s 12(4)(b))?
GIVEN `my election of the maximum number of weeks` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks` @desc Which maximum number of weeks did you elect for caring for a new-born or adopted child? One of: the 35-week maximum, the 61-week maximum.
      `the weeks of benefits are divided between two claimants under section 23` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the weeks of benefits for the same child or children divided between two claimants under section 23?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks can be paid for the care of my new-born or adopted child` IS
    `s 12(4)(b) the maximum number of weeks for the care of one or more new-born or adopted children as a result of a single pregnancy or placement` `my election of the maximum number of weeks` `the weeks of benefits are divided between two claimants under section 23`

-- s 12(4.01): where claims are made under this Part and under section 152.05 for the same child, the most under the Act as a whole is the same figure; NOTHING if there is not a claim under each.
@export What is the most weeks payable under the Act for my child when claims are made under both Parts (s 12(4.01))?
GIVEN `a claim is made under this Part and a claim is made under section 152.05 for the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a claim made under this Part and also a claim under section 152.05 (self-employed persons) for the same child or children?
      `my election of the maximum number of weeks` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks` @desc Which maximum number of weeks did you elect for caring for a new-born or adopted child? One of: the 35-week maximum, the 61-week maximum.
      `the weeks of benefits are divided between two claimants under section 23` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the weeks of benefits for the same child or children divided between two claimants under section 23?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most weeks payable under the Act for my child when claims are made under both Parts` IS
    `s 12(4.01) the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable under the Act in respect of the child or children` `a claim is made under this Part and a claim is made under section 152.05 for the same child or children` `my election of the maximum number of weeks` `the weeks of benefits are divided between two claimants under section 23`

-- s 12(4.1): all claims for the same reason about the same family member share 26 weeks in the 52 weeks (or a shorter prescribed period).
@export How many weeks of compassionate care benefits can still be paid for my family member (s 12(4.1))?
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits already paid or payable under the Act for my family member` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits have already been paid or are payable under all claims under the Act for the same reason in respect of this family member, during the period?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of compassionate care benefits can still be paid for my family member` IS
    `s 12(4.1) the weeks of benefits still payable in respect of the family member` `the weeks of benefits already paid or payable under the Act for my family member`

-- s 12(4.2): the 52 weeks are a shorter prescribed period if one is prescribed under subsection 23.1(5).
@export How many weeks long is the period for compassionate care benefits (s 12(4.2))?
GIVEN `a shorter period is prescribed for compassionate care benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a shorter period than 52 weeks prescribed for compassionate care benefits under subsection 23.1(5)?
      `the length in weeks of the shorter prescribed period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks long is the shorter prescribed period? Ignored if none is prescribed.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks long is the period for compassionate care benefits` IS
    `s 12(4.2) the length in weeks of the period of 52 weeks in subsection (4.1), or of the shorter period if one is prescribed` (IF `a shorter period is prescribed for compassionate care benefits` THEN JUST `the length in weeks of the shorter prescribed period` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 12(4.3): once a shorter period has expired for a family member, no further compassionate care benefits are payable until the minimum prescribed number of weeks has elapsed.
@export Are further compassionate care benefits payable for my family member (s 12(4.3))?
GIVEN `a shorter period has expired in respect of my family member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a shorter period under subsection 12(4.2) expired in respect of your family member?
      `the minimum prescribed number of weeks has elapsed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the minimum prescribed number of weeks elapsed since that shorter period expired?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are further compassionate care benefits payable for my family member` IF
    `s 12(4.3) further benefits are payable under section 23.1 in respect of the family member` `a shorter period has expired in respect of my family member` `the minimum prescribed number of weeks has elapsed`

-- s 12(4.4): all claims about the same critically ill child share 35 weeks in the 52 weeks.
@export How many weeks of benefits can still be paid for my critically ill child (s 12(4.4))?
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits already paid or payable under the Act for the critically ill child` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits have already been paid or are payable under all claims under the Act for the same reason in respect of this child, during the 52 weeks?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits can still be paid for my critically ill child` IS
    `s 12(4.4) the weeks of benefits still payable in respect of the critically ill child` `the weeks of benefits already paid or payable under the Act for the critically ill child`

-- s 12(4.5): all claims about the same critically ill adult share 15 weeks in the 52 weeks.
@export How many weeks of benefits can still be paid for my critically ill adult (s 12(4.5))?
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits already paid or payable under the Act for the critically ill adult` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits have already been paid or are payable under all claims under the Act for the same reason in respect of this adult, during the 52 weeks?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits can still be paid for my critically ill adult` IS
    `s 12(4.5) the weeks of benefits still payable in respect of the critically ill adult` `the weeks of benefits already paid or payable under the Act for the critically ill adult`

-- s 12(5): the most combined weeks of special benefits is 50, or, if my benefit period is extended under s 10(13), the s 10(15) length less two weeks.
@export What is the most number of combined weeks of special benefits I can be paid (s 12(5))?
GIVEN `my benefit period is extended under section 10(13)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your benefit period extended under subsection 10(13) (to pay special benefits up to the maximum total number of weeks)?
      `the maximum number of weeks in my benefit period calculated under section 10(15)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum number of weeks in your benefit period calculated under subsection 10(15) (the answer to "What is the longest my benefit period can be after an extension for special benefits")? Ignored unless your benefit period is extended under 10(13).
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most number of combined weeks of special benefits I can be paid` IS
    `s 12(5) the maximum number of combined weeks of benefits because of reasons mentioned in subsection (3)` `my benefit period is extended under section 10(13)` `the maximum number of weeks in my benefit period calculated under section 10(15)`

-- s 12(6): general and special weeks may be combined, but not more than 50 in total.
@export How many general and special weeks can I combine in total (s 12(6))?
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits I am entitled to under the general maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits are you entitled to under subsection 12(2), (2.1) or (2.3)?
      `the weeks of benefits I am entitled to because of a special reason` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits are you entitled to because of a reason mentioned in subsection 12(3)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many general and special weeks can I combine in total` IS
    `s 12(6) the total number of weeks of benefits that may be combined` `the weeks of benefits I am entitled to under the general maximum` `the weeks of benefits I am entitled to because of a special reason`

-- s 12(7): to see whether the total of s 12(6) has been reached, parental weeks at the 61-week maximum are converted to weeks at 55%, and weeks with no benefits paid are counted as paid
-- (except the extension weeks of s 10(10) to (12.1) and the waiting-period week).
@export How many weeks count toward my total number of weeks of benefits (s 12(7))?
GIVEN `the weeks of parental benefits paid at the 61-week maximum, converted to weeks at 55%` IS A NUMBER @desc Converted by the table in Schedule IV, how many weeks at a rate of weekly benefits of 55% are the weeks of parental benefits you were paid at the 61-week maximum (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of other benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of other benefits were you paid in your benefit period?
      `the weeks of my benefit period for which no benefits were paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of your benefit period had no benefits paid?
      `the weeks of extension of my benefit period under section 10(10) to (12.1)` IS A NUMBER @desc By how many weeks is your benefit period extended under subsections 10(10) to (12.1)?
      `the waiting-period week is among the weeks for which no benefits were paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your waiting-period week among the weeks for which no benefits were paid?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks count toward my total number of weeks of benefits` IS
    `s 12(7) the number of weeks that count toward the total number of weeks of benefits established under subsection (6)` `the weeks of parental benefits paid at the 61-week maximum, converted to weeks at 55%` `the weeks of other benefits I was paid` `the weeks of my benefit period for which no benefits were paid` `the weeks of extension of my benefit period under section 10(10) to (12.1)` `the waiting-period week is among the weeks for which no benefits were paid`

-- s 12(8): two or more children placed with a major attachment claimant for adoption at about the same time are a single placement.
@export Are the children placed with me for adoption a single placement (s 12(8))?
GIVEN `two or more children are placed with me for adoption at the same or substantially the same time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are two or more children placed with you, a major attachment claimant, for the purpose of adoption at the same or substantially the same time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the children placed with me for adoption a single placement` IF
    `s 12(8) the placement is a single placement of a child or children for the purpose of adoption` `two or more children are placed with me for adoption at the same or substantially the same time`

§§ `The waiting period (sections 13 and 13.1)`

-- Section 13: a one-week waiting period before benefits are paid.

-- s 13: I am not entitled to be paid benefits in my benefit period until I have served a waiting period of one week of unemployment for which benefits would otherwise be payable.
@export Am I entitled to be paid benefits yet, or must I still serve a waiting period (s 13)?
GIVEN `the weeks of unemployment I have served as a waiting period since my benefit period began` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of unemployment, for which benefits would otherwise be payable, have you served as a waiting period since the beginning of your benefit period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to be paid benefits yet` IF
    `s 13 the claimant is entitled to be paid benefits in the benefit period` (`s 13 the claimant has served a waiting period of one week of unemployment` `the weeks of unemployment I have served as a waiting period since my benefit period began`)

-- s 13.1: a week of unemployment counts as the waiting-period week if, were it not the waiting period, my benefit for it, after deducting earnings above $50 (rate under $200) or above 25% of the rate (rate of $200 or more), would be more than zero.
@export Does a week with earnings count as my waiting-period week (s 13.1)?
GIVEN `my weekly rate of benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your weekly rate of benefit, in dollars?
      `my earnings in the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your earnings in the week, as determined for the purpose of subsection 19(2), in dollars?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a week with earnings count as my waiting-period week` IF
    `s 13.1(1) the week of unemployment is deemed to be a week of unemployment for which benefits would otherwise be payable` `my weekly rate of benefit` `my earnings in the week`

§§ `How much I am paid each week (sections 14, 16 and 17)`

-- Sections 14, 16, 17: the weeks my earnings are averaged over, the weekly rate, the family supplement and the ceiling.

-- s 14(2) and (4): the calculation period is 22 weeks at a regional rate of 6% or less, 21 at more than 6% to 7%, and so on down to 14 at more than 13%.
@export How many weeks make up my calculation period (s 14(2), (4))?
GIVEN `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the regional rate of unemployment that applies to you, as a decimal fraction (6.5% is 0.065)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks make up my calculation period` IS
    `s 14(4) the number of weeks in the calculation period` `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me`

-- s 14(1.1): the maximum weekly insurable earnings is $750 for a benefit period beginning in 1997 to 2000 and later the maximum yearly insurable earnings divided by 52; NOTHING before 1997.
@export What is the most my weekly insurable earnings can be (s 14(1.1))?
GIVEN `the day my benefit period begins` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your benefit period begin (a Sunday), as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year in which your benefit period begins, in dollars (the published figure)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most my weekly insurable earnings can be` IS
    `s 14(1.1) the maximum weekly insurable earnings` `the day my benefit period begins` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year`

-- s 14(2), (3): my weekly insurable earnings are my insurable earnings in the calculation period (the highest-earning weeks, plus lay-off or separation pay) divided by the weeks of the
-- calculation period, but not more than the maximum weekly insurable earnings. NOTHING for a benefit period before 1997 (no maximum is given).
@export What are my weekly insurable earnings (s 14(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my insurable earnings in my calculation period, not counting pay by reason of lay-off or separation` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your insurable earnings in the calculation period (those of your highest-earning weeks in your qualifying period, as many weeks as your calculation period has), in dollars, not counting insurable earnings paid or payable by reason of lay-off or separation from employment?
      `the insurable earnings paid or payable to me by reason of lay-off or separation from employment during my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc What insurable earnings were paid or payable to you during your qualifying period by reason of lay-off or separation from employment, in dollars?
      `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the regional rate of unemployment that applies to you, as a decimal fraction (6.5% is 0.065)?
      `the day my benefit period begins` IS A DATE @desc On what date does your benefit period begin (a Sunday), as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year in which your benefit period begins, in dollars (the published figure)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my weekly insurable earnings` IS
    `s 14(2) the claimant's weekly insurable earnings` (`s 14(3) the insurable earnings in the calculation period` `my insurable earnings in my calculation period, not counting pay by reason of lay-off or separation` `the insurable earnings paid or payable to me by reason of lay-off or separation from employment during my qualifying period`) `the regional rate of unemployment that applies to me` (`s 14(1.1) the maximum weekly insurable earnings` `the day my benefit period begins` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year`)

-- ss 14(1) and 17: my weekly rate of benefits is 55% of my weekly insurable earnings (33% for the weeks of parental benefits at the 61-week maximum), rounded to the nearest dollar, and not above the maximum rate.
@export What is my weekly benefit rate (s 14(1), s 17)?
GIVEN `my weekly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your weekly insurable earnings, in dollars (the answer to "What are my weekly insurable earnings")?
      `I am paid benefits under section 23 for the week and my maximum is the 61 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid benefits under section 23 (parental benefits) for the week, and is your maximum number of weeks the 61 weeks of subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii)?
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year in which your benefit period begins, in dollars (the published figure)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my weekly benefit rate` IS
    `s 14(1) and s 17 the rate of weekly benefits, not above the maximum rate` (`s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits payable to the claimant` `my weekly insurable earnings` `I am paid benefits under section 23 for the week and my maximum is the 61 weeks`) (`s 17 the maximum rate of weekly benefits` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year`)

-- s 16: with one or more dependent children and low family income, my rate is increased by a family supplement, by no more than the prescribed percentage (25% if none) of my weekly insurable earnings.
@export By how much is my weekly rate increased by a family supplement (s 16)?
GIVEN `I have one or more dependent children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have one or more dependent children, as the Regulations define them?
      `I establish, in the manner the Commission directs, that I meet the prescribed low-income family eligibility criteria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you establish, in the manner the Commission directs, that you meet the prescribed low-income family eligibility criteria (regulation 34)?
      `the family supplement determined under the regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the family supplement determined in accordance with the regulations (regulation 34(5)), in dollars?
      `a percentage of my weekly insurable earnings is prescribed as the most the increase may be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a percentage of your weekly insurable earnings prescribed as the most the increase may be (regulation 34(6))? Answer no if none is prescribed.
      `the prescribed percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the prescribed percentage, as a decimal fraction (25% is 0.25)? Ignored if none is prescribed.
      `my weekly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your weekly insurable earnings, in dollars (the answer to "What are my weekly insurable earnings")?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By how much is my weekly rate increased by a family supplement` IS
    `s 16(1) and s 16(4) the amount of the increase in the rate of weekly benefits` (`s 16(1) the rate of weekly benefits is increased by the amount of a family supplement` `I have one or more dependent children` `I establish, in the manner the Commission directs, that I meet the prescribed low-income family eligibility criteria`) `the family supplement determined under the regulations` (`s 16(4) the most that the increase in the rate of weekly benefits may be` (IF `a percentage of my weekly insurable earnings is prescribed as the most the increase may be` THEN JUST `the prescribed percentage` ELSE NOTHING) `my weekly insurable earnings`)

-- s 17: the maximum rate of weekly benefits is 55% of the maximum yearly insurable earnings divided by 52, rounded to the nearest dollar.
@export What is the most I can be paid each week (s 17)?
GIVEN `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year in which your benefit period begins, in dollars (the published figure)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be paid each week` IS
    `s 17 the maximum rate of weekly benefits` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year`

§§ `When I am not entitled to be paid for a day (section 18)`

-- Section 18: I must prove I was available for work (or unable to work through illness, or on jury service) on each working day.

-- s 18(1) and (2): for each working day I must prove that I was capable of and available for work and unable to obtain suitable employment; or unable to work because of a prescribed
-- illness, injury or quarantine (and, unless benefits are payable under ss 23 to 23.3, that I would otherwise have been available); or engaged in jury service.
@export Am I entitled to be paid benefits for a working day, as far as section 18 goes (s 18)?
GIVEN `the day is a working day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day a working day (any day of the week except Saturday and Sunday)?
      `I was capable of work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you capable of work on that day?
      `I was available for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you available for work on that day?
      `I was unable to obtain suitable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you unable to obtain suitable employment on that day?
      `I was unable to work because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you unable to work on that day because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine?
      `I would otherwise have been available for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you otherwise have been available for work, were it not for the illness, injury or quarantine?
      `benefits are payable to me under any of sections 23 to 23.3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are benefits payable to you for caring for a new-born or adopted child, a family member, a critically ill child or a critically ill adult (sections 23 to 23.3)?
      `I was engaged in jury service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you engaged in jury service on that day?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to be paid benefits for a working day as far as section 18 goes` IF
    `s 18(1) the claimant is entitled to be paid benefits for the day as far as section 18 goes` `the day is a working day` (`s 18(1)(a) the claimant was capable of and available for work and unable to obtain suitable employment` `I was capable of work` `I was available for work` `I was unable to obtain suitable employment`) (`s 18(1)(b) and s 18(2) the claimant was unable to work because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` `I was unable to work because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` `I would otherwise have been available for work` `benefits are payable to me under any of sections 23 to 23.3`) (`s 18(1)(c) the claimant was engaged in jury service` `I was engaged in jury service`)

§§ `What is deducted from my benefits for earnings (section 19)`

-- Section 19: earnings in the waiting period, in other weeks, and earnings I failed to declare.

-- s 19(1): earnings during my waiting period are deducted, as the regulations prescribe, from the benefits for the first three weeks for which benefits are otherwise payable (never more than the earnings).
@export How much is deducted from my first three weeks of benefits for my waiting period earnings (s 19(1))?
GIVEN `my earnings during my waiting period` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your earnings during your waiting period, in dollars?
      `the amount the regulations prescribe be deducted for my waiting period earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount do the Regulations require to be deducted for your earnings in the waiting period (regulation 39: normally the earnings themselves, up to your weekly rate of benefits), in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is deducted from my first three weeks of benefits for my waiting period earnings` IS
    `s 19(1) the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks for which benefits are otherwise payable` `my earnings during my waiting period` `the amount the regulations prescribe be deducted for my waiting period earnings`

-- s 19(2): in any other week of unemployment, 50% of my earnings up to 90% of my weekly insurable earnings, and 100% of the earnings above that, are deducted from the benefits for the week.
@export How much is deducted from my benefits for earnings in a week of unemployment (s 19(2))?
GIVEN `my earnings in the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your earnings in the week, as determined for the purpose of subsection 19(2), in dollars?
      `my weekly insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your weekly insurable earnings, in dollars (the answer to "What are my weekly insurable earnings")?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is deducted from my benefits for earnings in a week of unemployment` IS
    `s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable in the week` `my earnings in the week` `my weekly insurable earnings`

@export What benefits are left for the week after the deduction for earnings (s 19(2))?
GIVEN `the benefits payable in the week before the deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the benefits payable for the week before any deduction for earnings, in dollars?
      `the amount deducted from the benefits payable in the week` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount is deducted from the benefits for the week for your earnings (the answer to "How much is deducted from my benefits for earnings in a week")?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What benefits are left for the week after the deduction for earnings` IS
    `s 19(2) the benefits payable in the week after the deduction` `the benefits payable in the week before the deduction` `the amount deducted from the benefits payable in the week`

-- s 19(3)(a): if I failed to declare earnings, the deduction is the whole of the undeclared earnings if the Commission is of the opinion that I knowingly failed to declare them;
-- otherwise the undeclared earnings less the difference between all the s 19(2) amounts for the period and those applied to the earnings I did declare.
@export How much is deducted for the earnings I failed to declare (s 19(3)(a))?
GIVEN `the Commission is of the opinion that I knowingly failed to declare my earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commission of the opinion that you knowingly failed to declare the earnings?
      `the amount of my undeclared earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of your undeclared earnings for the period, in dollars?
      `all the amounts that apply to my earnings for the period under section 19(2)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of all amounts that section 19(2) takes off your benefits for the period, counting all your earnings (declared and undeclared), in dollars?
      `the amounts applied under section 19(2) to my declared earnings for the period` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the amounts applied under section 19(2) to your declared earnings for the period, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is deducted for the earnings I failed to declare` IS
    `s 19(3)(a) the amount deducted from the benefits paid to the claimant for the period` `the Commission is of the opinion that I knowingly failed to declare my earnings` `the amount of my undeclared earnings` `all the amounts that apply to my earnings for the period under section 19(2)` `the amounts applied under section 19(2) to my declared earnings for the period`

-- s 19(3)(b): the deduction starts with the first week for which the earnings were not declared and takes the whole of the benefits paid for each consecutive week until it is used up.
-- This question looks at four weeks; an amount not used up in them continues into later weeks.
@export How is the deduction for my undeclared earnings spread over my weeks of benefits (s 19(3)(b))?
GIVEN `the amount still to be deducted for my undeclared earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount still to be deducted from your benefits for the undeclared earnings (the answer to "How much is deducted for my undeclared earnings"), in dollars?
      `the benefits paid to me for the 1st week, counting from the first week the earnings were not declared` IS A NUMBER @desc What benefits were paid to you for the first week for which the earnings were not declared, in dollars (0 if none)?
      `the benefits paid to me for the 2nd week` IS A NUMBER @desc What benefits were paid to you for the next week, in dollars (0 if none)?
      `the benefits paid to me for the 3rd week` IS A NUMBER @desc What benefits were paid to you for the third week, in dollars (0 if none)?
      `the benefits paid to me for the 4th week` IS A NUMBER @desc What benefits were paid to you for the fourth week, in dollars (0 if none)?
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `How is the deduction for my undeclared earnings spread over my weeks of benefits` IS
    `s 19(3)(b) the amount deducted in each consecutive week` `the amount still to be deducted for my undeclared earnings` (LIST `the benefits paid to me for the 1st week, counting from the first week the earnings were not declared`, `the benefits paid to me for the 2nd week`, `the benefits paid to me for the 3rd week`, `the benefits paid to me for the 4th week`)

-- s 19(4): earnings from an employment support measure (other than one in 59(c) or (d)) and allowances for a course or program are not deducted except as the regulations provide.
@export May my earnings or allowances from an employment support measure or a course be deducted (s 19(4))?
GIVEN `my earnings are from employment under an employment support measure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your earnings from employment under an employment support measure?
      `that measure is one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that measure one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d) of the Act?
      `my earnings or allowances are payable to me for attending a course or program of instruction or training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the earnings or allowances payable to you for attending a course or program of instruction or training?
      `the regulations provide for my earnings or allowances to be deducted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the Regulations provide for those earnings or allowances to be deducted?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my earnings or allowances from an employment support measure or a course be deducted` IF
    `s 19(4) the earnings or allowances may be deducted under section 19` `my earnings are from employment under an employment support measure` `that measure is one referred to in paragraph 59(c) or (d)` `my earnings or allowances are payable to me for attending a course or program of instruction or training` `the regulations provide for my earnings or allowances to be deducted`

§§ `What is deducted for days on which I am not entitled (section 20)`

-- Section 20: the deduction for working days on which I am not entitled to be paid.

-- s 20(1): for each working day in my waiting period on which I am not entitled to benefits, 1/5 of my weekly rate of benefits is deducted from the benefits for the three weeks of s 19(1).
@export How much is deducted for working days in my waiting period on which I am not entitled to benefits (s 20(1))?
GIVEN `my weekly rate of benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your weekly rate of benefit, in dollars?
      `the working days in my waiting period for which I am not entitled to receive benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many working days in your waiting period are you not entitled to receive benefits?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is deducted for working days in my waiting period on which I am not entitled to benefits` IS
    `s 20(1) the amount deducted for the excluded days in the waiting period` `my weekly rate of benefit` `the working days in my waiting period for which I am not entitled to receive benefits`

-- s 20(2): for each working day in another week of unemployment on which I am disentitled, 1/5 of my weekly rate of benefits is deducted from that week's benefits.
@export How much is deducted for working days in another week on which I am disentitled (s 20(2))?
GIVEN `my weekly rate of benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your weekly rate of benefit, in dollars?
      `the working days in my week of unemployment, not in the waiting period, for which I am disentitled` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many working days in a week of unemployment that is not in your waiting period are you disentitled from receiving benefits?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is deducted for working days in another week on which I am disentitled` IS
    `s 20(2) the amount deducted for the days of disentitlement in a week that is not in the waiting period` `my weekly rate of benefit` `the working days in my week of unemployment, not in the waiting period, for which I am disentitled`

§§ `Illness, injury or quarantine (section 21)`

-- Section 21: benefits for illness, injury or quarantine. Asked only if you are off work for that reason.

-- s 21(1): a minor attachment claimant (fewer than 600 hours) who ceases work because of illness, injury or quarantine is not entitled to benefits while unable to work for that reason.
@export Am I barred from sickness benefits as a minor attachment claimant (s 21(1))?
GIVEN `I qualify to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify to receive benefits (the answer to "Do I qualify for regular benefits")?
      `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period?
      `I cease work because of illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you ceased work because of illness, injury or quarantine?
      `I am unable to work for that reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you unable to work for that reason?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from sickness benefits as a minor attachment claimant` IF
    `s 21(1) the minor attachment claimant is not entitled to receive benefits while unable to work for that reason` (`s 6(1) minor attachment claimant` `I qualify to receive benefits` `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period`) `I cease work because of illness, injury or quarantine` `I am unable to work for that reason`

-- s 21(2): if benefits are payable for illness, injury or quarantine and allowances are payable under a provincial law, my benefits are reduced or eliminated as prescribed.
@export What are my sickness benefits after the reduction for provincial allowances (s 21(2))?
GIVEN `benefits are payable to me because of illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are benefits payable to you because of illness, injury or quarantine?
      `allowances, money or other benefits are payable to me for that under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any allowances, money or other benefits payable to you for that reason under a provincial law?
      `the benefits payable to me under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the benefits payable to you under the Act, in dollars?
      `the amount by which the regulations reduce my benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc By what amount do the Regulations reduce your benefits because of those allowances, in dollars? (For pregnancy and parental benefits under a provincial plan, regulations 76.16 and 76.17 deduct the provincial benefits; enter 0 if the Regulations prescribe no reduction.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my sickness benefits after the reduction for provincial allowances` IS
    `s 21(2) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` `benefits are payable to me because of illness, injury or quarantine` `allowances, money or other benefits are payable to me for that under a provincial law` `the benefits payable to me under the Act` `the amount by which the regulations reduce my benefits`

-- s 21(3): allowances payable to me for the week under my employer's plan, where the employer's premium has been reduced under regulations made under s 69(1), are deducted from my sickness benefits for the week.
@export What are my sickness benefits for a week after deducting my employer's plan (s 21(3))?
GIVEN `benefits are payable to me for the week because of illness, injury or quarantine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are benefits payable to you for the week because of illness, injury or quarantine?
      `the benefits payable in the week before the deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the benefits payable for the week before any deduction for earnings, in dollars?
      `the allowances, money or other benefits payable to me for the week under my employer's plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What allowances, money or other benefits are payable to you for the week under a plan that covers insured persons employed by your employer, in dollars?
      `my employer's premium has been reduced under regulations made under section 69(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer's premium been reduced in accordance with regulations made under subsection 69(1) because of that plan?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my sickness benefits for a week after deducting my employer's plan` IS
    `s 21(3) the benefits payable for the week after deducting the allowances payable under the employer's plan` `benefits are payable to me for the week because of illness, injury or quarantine` `the benefits payable in the week before the deduction` `the allowances, money or other benefits payable to me for the week under my employer's plan` `my employer's premium has been reduced under regulations made under section 69(1)`

§§ `Pregnancy (section 22)`

-- Section 22: maternity benefits. Asked only if you are pregnant or have given birth.

-- s 22(1): despite section 18, benefits are payable to a major attachment claimant (600 or more hours) who proves her pregnancy.
@export Are benefits payable to me because of my pregnancy (s 22(1))?
GIVEN `I qualify to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify to receive benefits (the answer to "Do I qualify for regular benefits")?
      `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period?
      `I prove my pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you prove your pregnancy?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are benefits payable to me because of my pregnancy` IF
    `s 22(1) benefits are payable to the claimant despite section 18` (`s 6(1) major attachment claimant` `I qualify to receive benefits` `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period`) `I prove my pregnancy`

-- s 22(2): the period begins with the earlier of the week 12 weeks before the week my confinement is expected and the week it occurs, and ends 17 weeks after the later of those two weeks.
@export On what date does my maternity benefit period begin (s 22(2))?
GIVEN `a day in the week my confinement is expected` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your confinement expected, as YYYY-MM-DD (any day of the expected week)?
      `my confinement has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your confinement occurred?
      `a day in the week my confinement occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your confinement occur, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored if it has not.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my maternity benefit period begin` IS
    (`s 22(2) the period during which benefits are payable` `a day in the week my confinement is expected` (IF `my confinement has occurred` THEN JUST `a day in the week my confinement occurred` ELSE NOTHING))'s `first day of the period`

@export On what date does my maternity benefit period end (s 22(2))?
GIVEN `a day in the week my confinement is expected` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your confinement expected, as YYYY-MM-DD (any day of the expected week)?
      `my confinement has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your confinement occurred?
      `a day in the week my confinement occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your confinement occur, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored if it has not.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my maternity benefit period end` IS
    (`s 22(2) the period during which benefits are payable` `a day in the week my confinement is expected` (IF `my confinement has occurred` THEN JUST `a day in the week my confinement occurred` ELSE NOTHING))'s `last day of the period`

-- s 22(3): if allowances are payable under a provincial law for the pregnancy, my benefits are reduced or eliminated as prescribed.
@export What are my maternity benefits after the reduction for provincial allowances (s 22(3))?
GIVEN `benefits are payable to me for unemployment caused by pregnancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are benefits payable to you for unemployment caused by pregnancy?
      `allowances, money or other benefits are payable to me for that under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any allowances, money or other benefits payable to you for that reason under a provincial law?
      `the benefits payable to me under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the benefits payable to you under the Act, in dollars?
      `the amount by which the regulations reduce my benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc By what amount do the Regulations reduce your benefits because of those allowances, in dollars? (For pregnancy and parental benefits under a provincial plan, regulations 76.16 and 76.17 deduct the provincial benefits; enter 0 if the Regulations prescribe no reduction.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my maternity benefits after the reduction for provincial allowances` IS
    `s 22(3) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` `benefits are payable to me for unemployment caused by pregnancy` `allowances, money or other benefits are payable to me for that under a provincial law` `the benefits payable to me under the Act` `the amount by which the regulations reduce my benefits`

-- s 22(4): for the purposes of the waiting period (s 13), section 18 does not apply to the week just before the maternity period.
@export Does section 18 not apply to this week for my waiting period (s 22(4))?
GIVEN `a day in the week my confinement is expected` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your confinement expected, as YYYY-MM-DD (any day of the expected week)?
      `my confinement has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your confinement occurred?
      `a day in the week my confinement occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your confinement occur, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored if it has not.
      `the Sunday of the week in question` IS A DATE @desc What is the Sunday of the week you are asking about, as YYYY-MM-DD?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 18 not apply to this week for my waiting period` IF
    `s 22(4) section 18 does not apply, for the purposes of section 13, to the week` (`s 22(2) the period during which benefits are payable` `a day in the week my confinement is expected` (IF `my confinement has occurred` THEN JUST `a day in the week my confinement occurred` ELSE NOTHING)) `the Sunday of the week in question`

-- s 22(5): allowances payable to me for the week under my employer's plan, where the employer's premium has been reduced, are deducted from my maternity benefits for the week.
@export What are my maternity benefits for a week after deducting my employer's plan (s 22(5))?
GIVEN `benefits are payable to me under section 22 for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are benefits payable to you for the week under section 22 (pregnancy)?
      `the benefits payable in the week before the deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the benefits payable for the week before any deduction for earnings, in dollars?
      `the allowances, money or other benefits payable to me for the week under my employer's plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What allowances, money or other benefits are payable to you for the week under a plan that covers insured persons employed by your employer, in dollars?
      `my employer's premium has been reduced under regulations made under section 69(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer's premium been reduced in accordance with regulations made under subsection 69(1) because of that plan?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my maternity benefits for a week after deducting my employer's plan` IS
    `s 22(5) the benefits payable for the week after deducting the allowances payable under the employer's plan` `benefits are payable to me under section 22 for the week` `the benefits payable in the week before the deduction` `the allowances, money or other benefits payable to me for the week under my employer's plan` `my employer's premium has been reduced under regulations made under section 69(1)`

-- s 22(6) and (7): if my child is in hospital the period is extended by the weeks in hospital, but ends no later than 52 weeks after the week of confinement.
@export On what date does my maternity benefit period end if my child is in hospital (s 22(6), (7))?
GIVEN `a day in the week my confinement is expected` IS A DATE @desc On what date is your confinement expected, as YYYY-MM-DD (any day of the expected week)?
      `my confinement has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your confinement occurred?
      `a day in the week my confinement occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date did your confinement occur, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored if it has not.
      `the weeks the child born of my pregnancy is in hospital` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks has the child born of your pregnancy been in hospital (0 if none)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my maternity benefit period end if my child is in hospital` IS
    (`s 22(6) and s 22(7) the period during which benefits are payable, extended` (`s 22(2) the period during which benefits are payable` `a day in the week my confinement is expected` (IF `my confinement has occurred` THEN JUST `a day in the week my confinement occurred` ELSE NOTHING)) `the weeks the child born of my pregnancy is in hospital` `a day in the week my confinement occurred`)'s `last day of the period`

§§ `Parental benefits (section 23)`

-- Section 23: benefits for caring for a new-born or adopted child. Asked only if you have a new-born or adopted child.

-- s 23(1): despite section 18, benefits are payable to a major attachment claimant to care for a new-born child of the claimant or a child placed with the claimant for adoption under the adoption law of the province of residence.
@export Are parental benefits payable to me (s 23(1))?
GIVEN `I qualify to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify to receive benefits (the answer to "Do I qualify for regular benefits")?
      `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period?
      `the benefits are to care for my new-born child or children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the benefits to care for one or more new-born children of yours?
      `the benefits are to care for a child placed with me for adoption under the law of my province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the benefits to care for one or more children placed with you for the purpose of adoption under the laws governing adoption in the province in which you reside?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are parental benefits payable to me` IF
    `s 23(1) benefits are payable to the claimant to care for one or more new-born or adopted children` (`s 6(1) major attachment claimant` `I qualify to receive benefits` `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period`) `the benefits are to care for my new-born child or children` `the benefits are to care for a child placed with me for adoption under the law of my province`

-- s 23(1.1): in my claim I must elect 35 or 61 weeks (subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) or (ii)).
@export How many weeks of parental benefits have I elected (s 23(1.1))?
GIVEN `my election of the maximum number of weeks` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks` @desc Which maximum number of weeks did you elect for caring for a new-born or adopted child? One of: the 35-week maximum, the 61-week maximum.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of parental benefits have I elected` IS
    `s 23(1.1) the maximum number of weeks elected` `my election of the maximum number of weeks`

-- s 23(1.2): my election is irrevocable once benefits are paid under section 23 or section 152.05 for the same child or children.
@export Is my election irrevocable (s 23(1.2))?
GIVEN `benefits have been paid under section 23 or 152.05 for the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have benefits been paid under section 23 or under section 152.05 in respect of the same child or children?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my election irrevocable` IF
    `s 23(1.2) the election is irrevocable` `benefits have been paid under section 23 or 152.05 for the same child or children`

-- s 23(1.3): where two claims are made for the same child or children, the election of the first to claim binds both claimants.
@export Which election binds me (s 23(1.3))?
GIVEN `my election of the maximum number of weeks` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks` @desc Which maximum number of weeks did you elect for caring for a new-born or adopted child? One of: the 35-week maximum, the 61-week maximum.
      `another claimant or individual has already claimed under section 23 or 152.05 for the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has another claimant (or a self-employed individual under section 152.05) already made a claim for the same child or children?
      `the election of the first to claim` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks` @desc What election did the first to claim make? One of: the 35-week maximum, the 61-week maximum. Ignored if nobody else has claimed.
GIVETH AN `Election of maximum weeks`
DECIDE `Which election binds me` IS
    `s 23(1.3) the election that binds the claimant` `my election of the maximum number of weeks` (IF `another claimant or individual has already claimed under section 23 or 152.05 for the same child or children` THEN JUST `the election of the first to claim` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 23(2): the period begins with the week my child is born or placed with me and ends 52 weeks after that week.
@export On what date does my parental benefit period begin (s 23(2))?
GIVEN `a day in the week my child was born or placed with me` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your child born, or placed with you for adoption, as YYYY-MM-DD?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my parental benefit period begin` IS
    (`s 23(2) the period during which benefits are payable` `a day in the week my child was born or placed with me`)'s `first day of the period`

@export On what date does my parental benefit period end (s 23(2))?
GIVEN `a day in the week my child was born or placed with me` IS A DATE @desc On what date was your child born, or placed with you for adoption, as YYYY-MM-DD?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my parental benefit period end` IS
    (`s 23(2) the period during which benefits are payable` `a day in the week my child was born or placed with me`)'s `last day of the period`

-- s 23(3), (3.01), (3.1), (3.2) to (3.4): the period of s 23(2) is extended by the weeks my child is in hospital and the weeks my parental leave is deferred or I am directed to return to duty
-- (together to at most 104 weeks), and, so that special benefits can be paid up to the maximum, by the extensions of (3.2), (3.21) and (3.22); never past 104 weeks or the s 10(15) length.
@export How many weeks long is my period for parental benefits (s 23(2) to (3.4))?
GIVEN `my child was in hospital during the period for parental benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your child, or were your children, in hospital during the period during which parental benefits are payable?
      `the weeks my child was in hospital` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks was your child, or were your children, in hospital? Ignored if not in hospital.
      `my parental leave was deferred or I was directed to return to duty under the National Defence Act regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc During the period during which parental benefits are payable, was the start of your parental leave deferred, or were you directed to return to duty from parental leave, under regulations made under the National Defence Act?
      `the weeks my parental leave was deferred or I was directed to return to duty` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks was your parental leave deferred or were you directed to return to duty? Ignored if not.
      `I was paid regular benefits in my benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you paid regular benefits during your benefit period?
      `the weeks of maternity benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits because of pregnancy in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of parental benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits for caring for a new-born or adopted child in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of sickness benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of compassionate care benefits I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits for the care or support of a family member in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill child I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits for the care or support of a critically ill child in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill adult I was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks were you paid benefits for the care or support of a critically ill adult in your benefit period (0 if none)?
      `my election of the maximum number of weeks` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks` @desc Which maximum number of weeks did you elect for caring for a new-born or adopted child? One of: the 35-week maximum, the 61-week maximum.
      `I was paid benefits for fewer than the total number of weeks established under section 12(6) as determined under section 12(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you paid benefits for fewer than the total number of weeks established under subsection 12(6), as determined under subsection 12(7)?
      `the weeks by which my benefit period must be extended to reach that total` IS A NUMBER @desc By how many weeks must your benefit period be extended so that benefits may be paid up to that total number of weeks (0 if none)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks long is my period for parental benefits` IS
    `s 23(2) to (3.4) the length of the period in weeks`
        (`s 23(3) the number of weeks by which the period is extended because the children are in hospital` `my child was in hospital during the period for parental benefits` `the weeks my child was in hospital`)
        (`s 23(3.01) the number of weeks by which the period is extended because of the Canadian Forces` `my parental leave was deferred or I was directed to return to duty under the National Defence Act regulations` `the weeks my parental leave was deferred or I was directed to return to duty`)
        (`s 23(3.2) the number of weeks by which the period is extended` (`s 23(3.2) the period is extended so that benefits may be paid up to the applicable maximum number of weeks` `I was paid regular benefits in my benefit period` `the special benefits I was paid` `my election of the maximum number of weeks`) `the special benefits I was paid` `my election of the maximum number of weeks`)
        (`s 23(3.21) the number of weeks by which the period is extended for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)` `parental benefits were paid` `my election of the maximum number of weeks` `I was paid regular benefits in my benefit period` `other special benefits were paid`)
        (`s 23(3.22) the number of weeks by which the period is extended for regular and special benefits` `I was paid regular benefits in my benefit period` `parental benefits were paid` `my election of the maximum number of weeks` `I was paid benefits for fewer than the total number of weeks established under section 12(6) as determined under section 12(7)` (`s 10(13.02) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended for regular and special benefits` `I was paid regular benefits in my benefit period` `parental benefits were paid` `my election of the maximum number of weeks` `I was paid benefits for fewer than the total number of weeks established under section 12(6) as determined under section 12(7)` `the weeks by which my benefit period must be extended to reach that total`))
        (`s 10(15) the maximum number of weeks in a benefit period extended under subsection (13)` `the special benefits I was paid` `my election of the maximum number of weeks`)
    WHERE
        `the special benefits I was paid` MEANS
            LIST (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `pregnancy`, `the weeks of maternity benefits I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `caring for a new-born or adopted child`, `the weeks of parental benefits I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine`, `the weeks of sickness benefits I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `care or support of a family member`, `the weeks of compassionate care benefits I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `care or support of a critically ill child`, `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill child I was paid`),
             (`ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason` OF `care or support of a critically ill adult`, `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill adult I was paid`)
        `parental benefits were paid` MEANS `the weeks of parental benefits I was paid` GREATER THAN 0
        `other special benefits were paid` MEANS
               `the weeks of maternity benefits I was paid` GREATER THAN 0
            OR `the weeks of sickness benefits I was paid` GREATER THAN 0
            OR `the weeks of compassionate care benefits I was paid` GREATER THAN 0
            OR `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill child I was paid` GREATER THAN 0
            OR `the weeks of benefits for a critically ill adult I was paid` GREATER THAN 0

-- s 23(3.5): if allowances are payable for the same reasons under a provincial law, my parental benefits are reduced or eliminated as prescribed.
@export What are my parental benefits after the reduction for provincial allowances (s 23(3.5))?
GIVEN `benefits are payable to me for the reasons set out in section 23` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are benefits payable to you for caring for a new-born or adopted child (the reasons set out in section 23)?
      `allowances, money or other benefits are payable to me for that under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any allowances, money or other benefits payable to you for that reason under a provincial law?
      `the benefits payable to me under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the benefits payable to you under the Act, in dollars?
      `the amount by which the regulations reduce my benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc By what amount do the Regulations reduce your benefits because of those allowances, in dollars? (For pregnancy and parental benefits under a provincial plan, regulations 76.16 and 76.17 deduct the provincial benefits; enter 0 if the Regulations prescribe no reduction.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my parental benefits after the reduction for provincial allowances` IS
    `s 23(3.5) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` `benefits are payable to me for the reasons set out in section 23` `allowances, money or other benefits are payable to me for that under a provincial law` `the benefits payable to me under the Act` `the amount by which the regulations reduce my benefits`

-- s 23(4), (4.1), (4.11): two claimants (two major attachment claimants, or one and a self-employed individual under s 152.05) may divide the weeks of benefits between them up to 40 weeks (35-week election)
-- or 69 weeks (61-week election), but neither may be paid more than 35 or 61 weeks; if they cannot agree the weeks are divided under the prescribed rules.
@export How many weeks of parental benefits may be divided between the other claimant and me (s 23(4), (4.1))?
GIVEN `my election of the maximum number of weeks` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks` @desc Which maximum number of weeks did you elect for caring for a new-born or adopted child? One of: the 35-week maximum, the 61-week maximum.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of parental benefits may be divided between the other claimant and me` IS
    `s 23(4) and s 23(4.1) the most weeks of benefits that may be divided between the claimants` `my election of the maximum number of weeks`

@export How many weeks of parental benefits may be paid to me alone (s 23(4.11))?
GIVEN `my election of the maximum number of weeks` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks` @desc Which maximum number of weeks did you elect for caring for a new-born or adopted child? One of: the 35-week maximum, the 61-week maximum.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of parental benefits may be paid to me alone` IS
    `s 23(4.11) the most weeks of benefits that may be paid to one claimant` `my election of the maximum number of weeks`

@export Is our division of the weeks of parental benefits within the limits (s 23(4))?
GIVEN `my election of the maximum number of weeks` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks` @desc Which maximum number of weeks did you elect for caring for a new-born or adopted child? One of: the 35-week maximum, the 61-week maximum.
      `the weeks of benefits divided to me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits are divided to you?
      `the weeks of benefits divided to the other claimant` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits are divided to the other claimant?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our division of the weeks of parental benefits within the limits` IF
    `s 23(4) the division of the weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limits` `my election of the maximum number of weeks` `the weeks of benefits divided to me` `the weeks of benefits divided to the other claimant`

@export Will our weeks of parental benefits be divided under the prescribed rules (s 23(4))?
GIVEN `we agree on a division of the weeks of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you and the other claimant agree on how to divide the weeks of benefits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will our weeks of parental benefits be divided under the prescribed rules` IF
    `s 23(4) the weeks of benefits are divided in accordance with the prescribed rules` `we agree on a division of the weeks of benefits`

-- s 23(5): a major attachment claimant may have the waiting period deferred until another claim in the same benefit period if a claim for the same child under section 22 or 23 has already served the waiting period,
-- or another claimant is serving it or elects to, or the prescribed requirements are met.
@export May I have my waiting period for parental benefits deferred (s 23(5))?
GIVEN `I qualify to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify to receive benefits (the answer to "Do I qualify for regular benefits")?
      `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period?
      `I have already made a claim under section 22 or 23 for the same child and have served the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already made a claim under section 22 or section 23 in respect of the same child and served the waiting period?
      `another major attachment claimant has claimed for the same child and has served or is serving their waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has another major attachment claimant made a claim under section 22 or section 23 in respect of the same child and served, or is serving, their waiting period?
      `another major attachment claimant is claiming for the same child at the same time and elects to serve the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is another major attachment claimant making a claim in respect of the same child at the same time as you and electing to serve the waiting period?
      `I or another major attachment claimant meet the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you or another major attachment claimant meet the prescribed requirements for deferring the waiting period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I have my waiting period for parental benefits deferred` IF
    `s 23(5) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` (`s 6(1) major attachment claimant` `I qualify to receive benefits` `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period`) `I have already made a claim under section 22 or 23 for the same child and have served the waiting period` `another major attachment claimant has claimed for the same child and has served or is serving their waiting period` `another major attachment claimant is claiming for the same child at the same time and elects to serve the waiting period` `I or another major attachment claimant meet the prescribed requirements`

-- s 23(6): where I (a major attachment claimant) and an individual claim for the same child and one has served or elected to serve the waiting period: if it was the individual, I need not serve one; if it was me, the individual may defer under section 152.05.
@export What happens to my waiting period when a self-employed person also claims for the same child (s 23(6))?
GIVEN `a major attachment claimant claims under section 22 or 23 and an individual claims under section 152.04 or 152.05 for the same child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, as a major attachment claimant, claim under section 22 or 23, and does an individual (a self-employed person) claim under section 152.04 or 152.05, for the same child or children?
      `one of us has served or elected to serve the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has one of you served, or elected to serve, the waiting period?
      `it is me, the major attachment claimant, who served or elected to serve the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it you, the major attachment claimant, who served or elected to serve the waiting period?
GIVETH A `ei1 Position of the waiting period under subsection 23(6)`
DECIDE `What happens to my waiting period when a self-employed person also claims for the same child` IS
    `s 23(6) the position of the waiting period when a major attachment claimant and an individual claim for the same child` `a major attachment claimant claims under section 22 or 23 and an individual claims under section 152.04 or 152.05 for the same child` `one of us has served or elected to serve the waiting period` `it is me, the major attachment claimant, who served or elected to serve the waiting period`

§§ `Caring for a family member (section 23.1)`

-- Section 23.1: compassionate care benefits. Asked only if you are caring for a family member with a serious medical condition and a significant risk of death.

-- s 23.1(2), (3), (5): benefits are payable to a major attachment claimant if a medical doctor or nurse practitioner (or, in the circumstances in the regulations, a member of a prescribed class) has issued a certificate that a family member has a serious medical condition
-- with a significant risk of death within 26 weeks (or a shorter prescribed period) and requires the care or support of other family members.
@export Are compassionate care benefits payable to me (s 23.1(2))?
GIVEN `I qualify to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify to receive benefits (the answer to "Do I qualify for regular benefits")?
      `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period?
      `a medical doctor or nurse practitioner has issued a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a medical doctor or nurse practitioner issued a certificate for the person you care for?
      `the practitioner who issued the certificate is a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate issued by an individual authorized by the government of a country other than Canada to do the work of a medical doctor or nurse practitioner, with substantially similar professional qualifications (regulation 41.2)?
      `the circumstances set out in the regulations for that practitioner exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the certificate refers to in that other country (the circumstance regulation 41.2 requires)?
      `the certificate states that a family member has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that a family member of yours has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within 26 weeks (or the shorter prescribed period)?
      `my family member requires the care or support of one or more other family members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that your family member requires the care or support of one or more other family members?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are compassionate care benefits payable to me` IF
    `s 23.1(2) benefits are payable to the claimant for the care or support of a family member` (`s 6(1) major attachment claimant` `I qualify to receive benefits` `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period`) `a medical doctor or nurse practitioner has issued a certificate` (`s 23.1(3) the certificate may be issued by a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners` `the practitioner who issued the certificate is a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners` `the circumstances set out in the regulations for that practitioner exist`) `the certificate states that a family member has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within the period` `my family member requires the care or support of one or more other family members`

-- s 23.1(2)(a) and (5)(a): the certificate must state a significant risk of death within 26 weeks, or within the shorter period if one is prescribed, counted from the day it is issued or from the earlier day it certifies from.
@export Does my certificate state a significant risk of death within the right period (s 23.1(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the weeks within which the certificate states there is a significant risk of death` IS A NUMBER @desc Within how many weeks does the certificate state that there is a significant risk of death for your family member, counted from the day the certificate is issued (or the earlier day from which it certifies the condition)?
      `a shorter period is prescribed for compassionate care benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a shorter period than 52 weeks prescribed for compassionate care benefits under subsection 23.1(5)?
      `the length in weeks of the shorter prescribed period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks long is the shorter prescribed period? Ignored if none is prescribed.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my certificate state a significant risk of death within the right period` IF
    `s 23.1(2)(a) the certificate states that a family member has a serious medical condition with a significant risk of death within the period` `the weeks within which the certificate states there is a significant risk of death` (IF `a shorter period is prescribed for compassionate care benefits` THEN JUST `the length in weeks of the shorter prescribed period` ELSE NOTHING)

@export May my certificate be issued by a member of a prescribed class of practitioners (s 23.1(3))?
GIVEN `the practitioner who issued the certificate is a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the certificate issued by an individual authorized by the government of a country other than Canada to do the work of a medical doctor or nurse practitioner, with substantially similar professional qualifications (regulation 41.2)?
      `the circumstances set out in the regulations for that practitioner exist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the certificate refers to in that other country (the circumstance regulation 41.2 requires)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my certificate be issued by a member of a prescribed class of practitioners` IF
    `s 23.1(3) the certificate may be issued by a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners` `the practitioner who issued the certificate is a member of a prescribed class of medical practitioners` `the circumstances set out in the regulations for that practitioner exist`

-- s 23.1(4): the period begins with the week of the day the first certificate is issued and filed (or, if I claimed first, the day the practitioner certifies from, or, if my claim is treated as made earlier under s 10(4) or (5), that earlier day) and ends with the week in which
-- benefits are exhausted, the family member dies, or 52 weeks (or the shorter prescribed period) end.
@export On what date does my compassionate care period begin (s 23.1(4))?
GIVEN `the day the first certificate was issued and filed with the Commission` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the first certificate that meets the requirements issued and filed with the Commission, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `I made my claim before the certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make your claim before the day the certificate was issued?
      `the day from which the practitioner certifies the condition` IS A DATE @desc From what date does the practitioner certify the condition, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless you made your claim before the certificate was issued.
      `my claim is regarded as made on an earlier day under section 10(4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim regarded as made on an earlier day under subsection 10(4) or (5)?
      `the earlier day on which my claim is regarded as made` IS A DATE @desc On what earlier date is your claim regarded as made, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless it is.
      `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time the claim is made, have all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to it already been exhausted?
      `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the beginning of the period during which benefits are payable for the person you care for already been determined?
      `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your claim have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date?
      `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations?
      `all the benefits payable for the person I care for have been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all the benefits payable in respect of the person you care for been exhausted?
      `the day those benefits were exhausted` IS A DATE @desc On what date were they exhausted, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless they have been.
      `the person I care for has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person you care for died?
      `the day the person I care for died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that person die, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless they have.
      `a shorter period is prescribed for compassionate care benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a shorter period than 52 weeks prescribed for compassionate care benefits under subsection 23.1(5)?
      `the length in weeks of the shorter prescribed period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks long is the shorter prescribed period? Ignored if none is prescribed.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my compassionate care period begin` IS
    (`s 23.1(4) the period during which benefits are payable` `the day the first certificate was issued and filed with the Commission` (IF `I made my claim before the certificate was issued` THEN JUST `the day from which the practitioner certifies the condition` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `my claim is regarded as made on an earlier day under section 10(4) or (5)` THEN JUST `the earlier day on which my claim is regarded as made` ELSE NOTHING) (`s 23.1(6) subparagraph (4)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`) (IF `all the benefits payable for the person I care for have been exhausted` THEN JUST `the day those benefits were exhausted` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `the person I care for has died` THEN JUST `the day the person I care for died` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `a shorter period is prescribed for compassionate care benefits` THEN JUST `the length in weeks of the shorter prescribed period` ELSE NOTHING))'s `first day of the period`

@export On what date does my compassionate care period end (s 23.1(4))?
GIVEN `the day the first certificate was issued and filed with the Commission` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the first certificate that meets the requirements issued and filed with the Commission, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `I made my claim before the certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make your claim before the day the certificate was issued?
      `the day from which the practitioner certifies the condition` IS A DATE @desc From what date does the practitioner certify the condition, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless you made your claim before the certificate was issued.
      `my claim is regarded as made on an earlier day under section 10(4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim regarded as made on an earlier day under subsection 10(4) or (5)?
      `the earlier day on which my claim is regarded as made` IS A DATE @desc On what earlier date is your claim regarded as made, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless it is.
      `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time the claim is made, have all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to it already been exhausted?
      `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the beginning of the period during which benefits are payable for the person you care for already been determined?
      `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your claim have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date?
      `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations?
      `all the benefits payable for the person I care for have been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all the benefits payable in respect of the person you care for been exhausted?
      `the day those benefits were exhausted` IS A DATE @desc On what date were they exhausted, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless they have been.
      `the person I care for has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person you care for died?
      `the day the person I care for died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did that person die, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless they have.
      `a shorter period is prescribed for compassionate care benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a shorter period than 52 weeks prescribed for compassionate care benefits under subsection 23.1(5)?
      `the length in weeks of the shorter prescribed period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks long is the shorter prescribed period? Ignored if none is prescribed.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my compassionate care period end` IS
    (`s 23.1(4) the period during which benefits are payable` `the day the first certificate was issued and filed with the Commission` (IF `I made my claim before the certificate was issued` THEN JUST `the day from which the practitioner certifies the condition` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `my claim is regarded as made on an earlier day under section 10(4) or (5)` THEN JUST `the earlier day on which my claim is regarded as made` ELSE NOTHING) (`s 23.1(6) subparagraph (4)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`) (IF `all the benefits payable for the person I care for have been exhausted` THEN JUST `the day those benefits were exhausted` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `the person I care for has died` THEN JUST `the day the person I care for died` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `a shorter period is prescribed for compassionate care benefits` THEN JUST `the length in weeks of the shorter prescribed period` ELSE NOTHING))'s `last day of the period`

-- s 23.1(4.1): a further certificate is needed after 26 weeks only if section 50(8.1) requires one.
@export Do I need a further certificate after 26 weeks (s 23.1(4.1))?
GIVEN `section 50(8.1) requires a further certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does subsection 50(8.1) require a further certificate for benefits after the first 26 weeks?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I need a further certificate after 26 weeks` IF
    `s 23.1(4.1) an additional certificate is needed for benefits payable after the end of the period of 26 weeks` `section 50(8.1) requires a further certificate`

-- s 23.1(6): subparagraph (4)(a)(ii) (counting the period from the day the practitioner certifies) does not apply if all benefits have been exhausted when the certificate is filed, if the period has already begun and the filing would move it earlier, or in other circumstances in the regulations.
@export Is my compassionate care period not counted from an earlier certified day (s 23.1(6))?
GIVEN `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time the claim is made, have all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to it already been exhausted?
      `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the beginning of the period during which benefits are payable for the person you care for already been determined?
      `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your claim have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date?
      `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my compassionate care period not counted from an earlier certified day` IF
    `s 23.1(6) subparagraph (4)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`

-- s 23.1(7): a claimant may have the waiting period deferred until another claim in the same benefit period if another claimant has already served (or is serving) theirs for the same family member, is claiming at the same time and elects to serve theirs, or the prescribed requirements are met.
@export May I have my waiting period deferred when I care for my family member (s 23.1(7))?
GIVEN `I make a claim for benefits under section 23.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make a claim for compassionate care benefits under section 23.1?
      `another claimant has claimed for the same family member and has served or is serving their waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has another claimant made a claim under section 23.1 or 152.06 in respect of the same family member during the period and served, or is serving, their waiting period?
      `another claimant is claiming for the same family member at the same time and elects to serve the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is another claimant making a claim under section 23.1 or 152.06 in respect of the same family member at the same time as you and electing to serve the waiting period?
      `the claimant or another claimant meets the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, or another claimant who has claimed for the same person, meet the prescribed requirements?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I have my waiting period deferred under section 23.1(7)` IF
    `s 23.1(7) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` `I make a claim for benefits under section 23.1` `another claimant has claimed for the same family member and has served or is serving their waiting period` `another claimant is claiming for the same family member at the same time and elects to serve the waiting period` `the claimant or another claimant meets the prescribed requirements`

@export How many weeks of benefits may be divided between the other claimant and me for my family member (s 23.1(8), (9))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits may be divided between the other claimant and me for my family member` IS
    `s 23.1(8) the most weeks of benefits that may be divided between the claimants`

@export Is our division of the remaining weeks for my family member within the limit (s 23.1(8), (9))?
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits divided to me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits are divided to you?
      `the weeks of benefits divided to the other claimant` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits are divided to the other claimant?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our division of the remaining weeks for my family member within the limit` IF
    `s 23.1(8) the division of the remaining weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limit` `the weeks of benefits divided to me` `the weeks of benefits divided to the other claimant`

@export Will our weeks for my family member be divided under the prescribed rules (s 23.1(8), (9))?
GIVEN `we agree on a division of the weeks of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you and the other claimant agree on how to divide the weeks of benefits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will our weeks for my family member be divided under the prescribed rules` IF
    `s 23.1(9) the weeks of benefits are divided in accordance with the prescribed rules` `we agree on a division of the weeks of benefits`

@export What are my compassionate care benefits after the reduction for provincial allowances (s 23.1(10))?
GIVEN `benefits are payable to me for the reasons set out in section 23.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are benefits payable to you for the reasons set out in section 23.1 (compassionate care)?
      `allowances, money or other benefits are payable to me for the same or substantially the same reasons under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any allowances, money or other benefits payable to you under a provincial law for the same or substantially the same reasons?
      `the benefits payable to me under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the benefits payable to you under the Act, in dollars?
      `the amount by which the regulations reduce my benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc By what amount do the Regulations reduce your benefits because of those allowances, in dollars? (For pregnancy and parental benefits under a provincial plan, regulations 76.16 and 76.17 deduct the provincial benefits; enter 0 if the Regulations prescribe no reduction.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my compassionate care benefits after the reduction for provincial allowances` IS
    `s 23.1(10) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` `benefits are payable to me for the reasons set out in section 23.1` `allowances, money or other benefits are payable to me for the same or substantially the same reasons under a provincial law` `the benefits payable to me under the Act` `the amount by which the regulations reduce my benefits`

§§ `Caring for a critically ill child (section 23.2)`

-- Section 23.2: benefits for caring for a critically ill child. Asked only if you are caring for a critically ill child.

-- s 23.2(1), (2): despite section 18, benefits are payable to a major attachment claimant who is a family member of a critically ill child, to care for or support that child, if a medical doctor or nurse practitioner (or a prescribed practitioner) has issued a certificate
-- stating that the child is critically ill and needs family care or support, and the period during which it is needed.
@export Are benefits payable to me for caring for a critically ill child (s 23.2(1))?
GIVEN `I qualify to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify to receive benefits (the answer to "Do I qualify for regular benefits")?
      `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period?
      `I am a family member of a critically ill child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a family member (as the Regulations define it) of a critically ill child (as the Regulations define it)?
      `the benefits are to care for or support that child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the benefits to care for or support that child?
      `a medical doctor, nurse practitioner or prescribed practitioner has issued a certificate for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a medical doctor or nurse practitioner issued a certificate for the child (or, if the child is in another country, an individual authorized there to do that work, under regulation 41.2)?
      `the certificate states that the child is critically ill and requires care or support from family members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that the child is a critically ill child and requires the care or support of one or more of their family members?
      `the certificate sets out the period during which care or support is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate set out the period during which care or support is required?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are benefits payable to me for caring for a critically ill child` IF
    `s 23.2(1) benefits are payable to the claimant to care for or support a critically ill child` (`s 6(1) major attachment claimant` `I qualify to receive benefits` `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period`) `I am a family member of a critically ill child` `the benefits are to care for or support that child` `a medical doctor, nurse practitioner or prescribed practitioner has issued a certificate for the child` `the certificate states that the child is critically ill and requires care or support from family members` `the certificate sets out the period during which care or support is required`

-- s 23.2(3): the period begins with the week of the day the first certificate is issued and filed (or the day the practitioner certifies from, if I claimed first, unless s 23.2(5) applies) and ends with the week in which benefits are exhausted, the child dies, or 52 weeks end.
@export On what date does my critically-ill-child period begin (s 23.2(3))?
GIVEN `the day the first certificate for the child was issued and filed with the Commission` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the first certificate for the child that meets the requirements issued and filed with the Commission, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `I made my claim for the child before the certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make your claim before the day the certificate for the child was issued?
      `the day from which the practitioner certifies that the child is critically ill` IS A DATE @desc From what date does the practitioner certify that the child is critically ill, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless you made your claim before the certificate was issued.
      `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time the claim is made, have all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to it already been exhausted?
      `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the beginning of the period during which benefits are payable for the person you care for already been determined?
      `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your claim have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date?
      `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations?
      `all the benefits payable for the child have been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all the benefits payable in respect of the child been exhausted?
      `the day the benefits for the child were exhausted` IS A DATE @desc On what date were they exhausted, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless they have been.
      `the child has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the child died?
      `the day the child died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the child die, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless the child has.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my critically-ill-child period begin` IS
    (`s 23.2(3) the period during which benefits are payable` `the day the first certificate for the child was issued and filed with the Commission` (IF `I made my claim for the child before the certificate was issued` THEN JUST `the day from which the practitioner certifies that the child is critically ill` ELSE NOTHING) (`s 23.2(5) subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`) (IF `all the benefits payable for the child have been exhausted` THEN JUST `the day the benefits for the child were exhausted` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `the child has died` THEN JUST `the day the child died` ELSE NOTHING))'s `first day of the period`

@export On what date does my critically-ill-child period end (s 23.2(3))?
GIVEN `the day the first certificate for the child was issued and filed with the Commission` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the first certificate for the child that meets the requirements issued and filed with the Commission, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `I made my claim for the child before the certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make your claim before the day the certificate for the child was issued?
      `the day from which the practitioner certifies that the child is critically ill` IS A DATE @desc From what date does the practitioner certify that the child is critically ill, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless you made your claim before the certificate was issued.
      `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time the claim is made, have all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to it already been exhausted?
      `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the beginning of the period during which benefits are payable for the person you care for already been determined?
      `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your claim have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date?
      `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations?
      `all the benefits payable for the child have been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all the benefits payable in respect of the child been exhausted?
      `the day the benefits for the child were exhausted` IS A DATE @desc On what date were they exhausted, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless they have been.
      `the child has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the child died?
      `the day the child died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the child die, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless the child has.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my critically-ill-child period end` IS
    (`s 23.2(3) the period during which benefits are payable` `the day the first certificate for the child was issued and filed with the Commission` (IF `I made my claim for the child before the certificate was issued` THEN JUST `the day from which the practitioner certifies that the child is critically ill` ELSE NOTHING) (`s 23.2(5) subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`) (IF `all the benefits payable for the child have been exhausted` THEN JUST `the day the benefits for the child were exhausted` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `the child has died` THEN JUST `the day the child died` ELSE NOTHING))'s `last day of the period`

-- s 23.2(5): subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply if benefits are exhausted when the certificate is filed, if the period has already begun and the filing would move it earlier, or in other circumstances in the regulations.
@export Is my critically-ill-child period not counted from an earlier certified day (s 23.2(5))?
GIVEN `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time the claim is made, have all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to it already been exhausted?
      `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the beginning of the period during which benefits are payable for the person you care for already been determined?
      `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your claim have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date?
      `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my critically-ill-child period not counted from an earlier certified day` IF
    `s 23.2(5) subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`

-- s 23.2(6): a claimant may have the waiting period deferred until another claim in the same benefit period if another claimant has already served (or is serving) theirs for the same critically ill child, is claiming at the same time and elects to serve theirs, or the prescribed requirements are met.
@export May I have my waiting period deferred when I care for my critically ill child (s 23.2(6))?
GIVEN `I make a claim for benefits under section 23.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make a claim for benefits for a critically ill child under section 23.2?
      `another claimant has claimed for the same child and has served or is serving their waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has another claimant made a claim under section 23.2 or 152.061 in respect of the same child during the period and served, or is serving, their waiting period?
      `another claimant is claiming for the same child at the same time and elects to serve the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is another claimant making a claim under section 23.2 or 152.061 in respect of the same child at the same time as you and electing to serve their waiting period?
      `the claimant or another claimant meets the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, or another claimant who has claimed for the same person, meet the prescribed requirements?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I have my waiting period deferred under section 23.2(6)` IF
    `s 23.2(6) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` `I make a claim for benefits under section 23.2` `another claimant has claimed for the same child and has served or is serving their waiting period` `another claimant is claiming for the same child at the same time and elects to serve the waiting period` `the claimant or another claimant meets the prescribed requirements`

@export How many weeks of benefits may be divided between the other claimant and me for my critically ill child (s 23.2(8), (9))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of benefits may be divided between the other claimant and me for my critically ill child` IS
    `s 23.2(8) the most weeks of benefits that may be divided between the claimants`

@export Is our division of the remaining weeks for my critically ill child within the limit (s 23.2(8), (9))?
GIVEN `the weeks of benefits divided to me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits are divided to you?
      `the weeks of benefits divided to the other claimant` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits are divided to the other claimant?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our division of the remaining weeks for my critically ill child within the limit` IF
    `s 23.2(8) the division of the remaining weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limit` `the weeks of benefits divided to me` `the weeks of benefits divided to the other claimant`

@export Will our weeks for my critically ill child be divided under the prescribed rules (s 23.2(8), (9))?
GIVEN `we agree on a division of the weeks of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you and the other claimant agree on how to divide the weeks of benefits?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will our weeks for my critically ill child be divided under the prescribed rules` IF
    `s 23.2(8) the weeks of benefits are divided in accordance with the prescribed rules` `we agree on a division of the weeks of benefits`

-- s 23.2(10): benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are not payable in respect of the child during the critically-ill-child period for that child.
@export Are compassionate care benefits payable for this child this week (s 23.2(10))?
GIVEN `the week falls in the period under section 23.2(3) or 152.061(3) for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the week fall in the period during which benefits for a critically ill child are payable for that child (under section 23.2(3) or 152.061(3))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are compassionate care benefits payable for this child this week` IF
    `s 23.2(10) benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are payable in respect of the child for the week` `the week falls in the period under section 23.2(3) or 152.061(3) for the child`

-- s 23.2(10.1): benefits under section 23.3 or 152.062 are not payable for a person during the 52 weeks of the critically-ill-child period if benefits were paid for that person under section 23.2.
@export Are critically-ill-adult benefits payable for me this week, having been a critically ill child (s 23.2(10.1))?
GIVEN `benefits were paid for me under section 23.2 when I was a critically ill child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were benefits paid under section 23.2 for you when you were a critically ill child?
      `the week falls in the 52 weeks from the first day of the week in which the child period began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the week fall in the period of 52 weeks that begins on the first day of the week with which your critically-ill-child period began?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are critically-ill-adult benefits payable for me this week having been a critically ill child` IF
    `s 23.2(10.1) benefits under section 23.3 or 152.062 are payable in respect of the person for the week` `benefits were paid for me under section 23.2 when I was a critically ill child` `the week falls in the 52 weeks from the first day of the week in which the child period began`

@export What are my critically-ill-child benefits after the reduction for provincial allowances (s 23.2(11))?
GIVEN `benefits are payable to me for the reasons set out in section 23.2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are benefits payable to you for the reasons set out in section 23.2 (critically ill child)?
      `allowances, money or other benefits are payable to me for the same or substantially the same reasons under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any allowances, money or other benefits payable to you under a provincial law for the same or substantially the same reasons?
      `the benefits payable to me under the Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What are the benefits payable to you under the Act, in dollars?
      `the amount by which the regulations reduce my benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc By what amount do the Regulations reduce your benefits because of those allowances, in dollars? (For pregnancy and parental benefits under a provincial plan, regulations 76.16 and 76.17 deduct the provincial benefits; enter 0 if the Regulations prescribe no reduction.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my critically-ill-child benefits after the reduction for provincial allowances` IS
    `s 23.2(11) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` `benefits are payable to me for the reasons set out in section 23.2` `allowances, money or other benefits are payable to me for the same or substantially the same reasons under a provincial law` `the benefits payable to me under the Act` `the amount by which the regulations reduce my benefits`

§§ `Caring for a critically ill adult (section 23.3, subsections 1 to 5)`

-- Section 23.3(1) to (5): benefits for caring for a critically ill adult. Asked only if you are caring for a critically ill adult. (Subsections (6) onward are in another piece of this encoding.)

-- s 23.3(1), (2): as s 23.2(1), for a critically ill adult.
@export Are benefits payable to me for caring for a critically ill adult (s 23.3(1))?
GIVEN `I qualify to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you qualify to receive benefits (the answer to "Do I qualify for regular benefits")?
      `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment do you have in your qualifying period?
      `I am a family member of a critically ill adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a family member (as the Regulations define it) of a critically ill adult (as the Regulations define it)?
      `the benefits are to care for or support that adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the benefits to care for or support that adult?
      `a medical doctor, nurse practitioner or prescribed practitioner has issued a certificate for the adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a medical doctor or nurse practitioner issued a certificate for the adult (or, if the adult is in another country, an individual authorized there to do that work, under regulation 41.2)?
      `the certificate states that the adult is critically ill and requires care or support from family members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state that the adult is a critically ill adult and requires the care or support of one or more of their family members?
      `the certificate sets out the period during which care or support is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate set out the period during which care or support is required?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are benefits payable to me for caring for a critically ill adult` IF
    `s 23.3(1) benefits are payable to the claimant to care for or support a critically ill adult` (`s 6(1) major attachment claimant` `I qualify to receive benefits` `the hours of insurable employment in my qualifying period`) `I am a family member of a critically ill adult` `the benefits are to care for or support that adult` `a medical doctor, nurse practitioner or prescribed practitioner has issued a certificate for the adult` `the certificate states that the adult is critically ill and requires care or support from family members` `the certificate sets out the period during which care or support is required`

-- s 23.3(3): as s 23.2(3), for a critically ill adult.
@export On what date does my critically-ill-adult period begin (s 23.3(3))?
GIVEN `the day the first certificate for the adult was issued and filed with the Commission` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the first certificate for the adult that meets the requirements issued and filed with the Commission, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `I made my claim for the adult before the certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make your claim before the day the certificate for the adult was issued?
      `the day from which the practitioner certifies that the adult is critically ill` IS A DATE @desc From what date does the practitioner certify that the adult is critically ill, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless you made your claim before the certificate was issued.
      `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time the claim is made, have all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to it already been exhausted?
      `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the beginning of the period during which benefits are payable for the person you care for already been determined?
      `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your claim have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date?
      `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations?
      `all the benefits payable for the adult have been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all the benefits payable in respect of the adult been exhausted?
      `the day the benefits for the adult were exhausted` IS A DATE @desc On what date were they exhausted, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless they have been.
      `the adult has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the adult died?
      `the day the adult died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the adult die, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless the adult has.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my critically-ill-adult period begin` IS
    (`s 23.3(3) the period during which benefits are payable` `the day the first certificate for the adult was issued and filed with the Commission` (IF `I made my claim for the adult before the certificate was issued` THEN JUST `the day from which the practitioner certifies that the adult is critically ill` ELSE NOTHING) (`s 23.3(4) subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`) (IF `all the benefits payable for the adult have been exhausted` THEN JUST `the day the benefits for the adult were exhausted` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `the adult has died` THEN JUST `the day the adult died` ELSE NOTHING))'s `first day of the period`

@export On what date does my critically-ill-adult period end (s 23.3(3))?
GIVEN `the day the first certificate for the adult was issued and filed with the Commission` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the first certificate for the adult that meets the requirements issued and filed with the Commission, as YYYY-MM-DD?
      `I made my claim for the adult before the certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make your claim before the day the certificate for the adult was issued?
      `the day from which the practitioner certifies that the adult is critically ill` IS A DATE @desc From what date does the practitioner certify that the adult is critically ill, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless you made your claim before the certificate was issued.
      `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time the claim is made, have all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to it already been exhausted?
      `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the beginning of the period during which benefits are payable for the person you care for already been determined?
      `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your claim have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date?
      `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations?
      `all the benefits payable for the adult have been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all the benefits payable in respect of the adult been exhausted?
      `the day the benefits for the adult were exhausted` IS A DATE @desc On what date were they exhausted, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless they have been.
      `the adult has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the adult died?
      `the day the adult died` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the adult die, as YYYY-MM-DD? Ignored unless the adult has.
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what date does my critically-ill-adult period end` IS
    (`s 23.3(3) the period during which benefits are payable` `the day the first certificate for the adult was issued and filed with the Commission` (IF `I made my claim for the adult before the certificate was issued` THEN JUST `the day from which the practitioner certifies that the adult is critically ill` ELSE NOTHING) (`s 23.3(4) subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`) (IF `all the benefits payable for the adult have been exhausted` THEN JUST `the day the benefits for the adult were exhausted` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `the adult has died` THEN JUST `the day the adult died` ELSE NOTHING))'s `last day of the period`

-- s 23.3(4): as s 23.2(5), for a critically ill adult.
@export Is my critically-ill-adult period not counted from an earlier certified day (s 23.3(4))?
GIVEN `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time the claim is made, have all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to it already been exhausted?
      `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the beginning of the period during which benefits are payable for the person you care for already been determined?
      `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would your claim have the effect of moving the beginning of that period to an earlier date?
      `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my critically-ill-adult period not counted from an earlier certified day` IF
    `s 23.3(4) subparagraph (3)(a)(ii) does not apply to the claim` `all the benefits that may otherwise have been payable in relation to my claim have already been exhausted` `the beginning of the period for the person I care for has already been determined` `my claim would move the beginning of that period to an earlier date` `my claim is made in any other circumstances set out in the regulations`

-- s 23.3(5): a claimant may have the waiting period deferred until another claim in the same benefit period if another claimant has already served (or is serving) theirs for the same critically ill adult, is claiming at the same time and elects to serve theirs, or the prescribed requirements are met.
@export May I have my waiting period deferred when I care for my critically ill adult (s 23.3(5))?
GIVEN `I make a claim for benefits under section 23.3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make a claim for benefits for a critically ill adult under section 23.3?
      `another claimant has claimed for the same adult and has served or is serving their waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has another claimant made a claim under section 23.3 or 152.062 in respect of the same adult during the period and served, or is serving, their waiting period?
      `another claimant is claiming for the same adult at the same time and elects to serve the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is another claimant making a claim under section 23.3 or 152.062 in respect of the same adult at the same time as you and electing to serve their waiting period?
      `the claimant or another claimant meets the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, or another claimant who has claimed for the same person, meet the prescribed requirements?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I have my waiting period deferred under section 23.3(5)` IF
    `s 23.3(5) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` `I make a claim for benefits under section 23.3` `another claimant has claimed for the same adult and has served or is serving their waiting period` `another claimant is claiming for the same adult at the same time and elects to serve the waiting period` `the claimant or another claimant meets the prescribed requirements`
